{
  "title": "5: Al-Ma'idah المائدة",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اَوْفُوْا بِالْعُقُوْدِ ؕ اُحِلَّتْ لَكُمْ بَهِيْمَةُ الْاَنْعَامِ اِلَّا مَا يُتْلٰى عَلَيْكُمْ غَيْرَ مُحِلِّى الصَّيْدِ وَاَنْتُمْ حُرُمٌ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَحْكُمُ مَا يُرِيْدُ‏(1)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO AWFOO BIL-O’QOOD, OHILLAT LAKUM BAHEEMATUL AN-A’AME ILLAA MAA YUTLAA A’LAYKUM GHAYRA MOHILLIS SAYDE WA ANTUM HOROM, INNAL LAAHA YAHKOMO MAA YOREED.\nO you who have faith! Keep your agreements. You are permitted animals of grazing livestock, except what is [now] announced to you, disallowing game while you are in pilgrim sanctity. Indeed Allah decrees whatever He desires.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تُحِلُّوْا شَعَآئِرَ اللّٰهِ وَلَا الشَّهْرَ الْحَرَامَ وَلَا الْهَدْىَ وَلَا الْقَلَٓائِدَ وَلَاۤ آٰمِّيْنَ الْبَيْتَ الْحَرَامَ يَبْتَغُوْنَ فَضْلًا مِّنْ رَّبِّهِمْ وَرِضْوَانًا ؕ وَاِذَا حَلَلْتُمْ فَاصْطَادُوْا ؕ وَلَا يَجْرِمَنَّكُمْ شَنَاٰنُ قَوْمٍ اَنْ صَدُّوْكُمْ عَنِ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ اَنْ تَعْتَدُوْا ۘ وَتَعَاوَنُوْا عَلَى الْبِرِّ وَالتَّقْوٰى وَلَا تَعَاوَنُوْا عَلَى الْاِثْمِ وَالْعُدْوَانِ وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ شَدِيْدُ الْعِقَابِ‏(2)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA TOHILLOO SHA-A’AA-ERAL LAAHE WA LASH SHAHRAL HARAAMA WA LAL HADYA WA LAL QALAAA-EDA WA LAA AAMMEENAL BAYTAL HARAAMA YABTAGHOONA FAZLAM MIR RABBEHIM WA RIZWAANAA, WA EZAA HALALTUM FASTAADOO, WA LAA YAJREMANNAKUM SHANA-AANO QAWMIN AN SADDOOKUM A’NIL MASJEDIL HARAAME AN TA’TADOO, WA TA-A’AWANOO A’LAL BIRRE WAT TAQWAA, WA LAA TA-A’AWANOO A’LAL ISME WAL U’DWAAN, WAT TAQUL LAAH, INNAL LAAHA SHADEEDUL E’QAAB.\nO you who have faith! Do not violate Allah’s sacraments, neither the sacred month, nor the offering, nor the necklaces, nor those bound for the Sacred House, who seek their Lord’s grace and [His] pleasure. But when you emerge from pilgrim sanctity, you may hunt for game. Ill feeling for a people should not lead you, because they barred you from [access to] the Sacred Mosque, to transgress. Cooperate in piety and Godwariness, but do not cooperate in sin and aggression, and be wary of Allah. Indeed Allah is severe in retribution.\nحُرِّمَتْ عَلَيْكُمُ الْمَيْتَةُ وَالدَّمُ وَلَحْمُ الْخِنْزِيْرِ وَمَاۤ اُهِلَّ لِغَيْرِ اللّٰهِ بِهٖ وَالْمُنْخَنِقَةُ وَالْمَوْقُوْذَةُ وَالْمُتَرَدِّيَةُ وَالنَّطِيْحَةُ وَمَاۤ اَكَلَ السَّبُعُ اِلَّا مَا ذَكَّيْتُمْ وَمَا ذُ بِحَ عَلَى النُّصُبِ وَاَنْ تَسْتَقْسِمُوْا بِالْاَزْلَامِ ؕ ذٰ لِكُمْ فِسْقٌ ؕ اَلْيَوْمَ يَئِسَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْ دِيْنِكُمْ فَلَا تَخْشَوْهُمْ وَاخْشَوْنِ ؕ اَلْيَوْمَ اَكْمَلْتُ لَكُمْ دِيْنَكُمْ وَاَ تْمَمْتُ عَلَيْكُمْ نِعْمَتِىْ وَرَضِيْتُ لَكُمُ الْاِسْلَامَ دِيْنًا ؕ فَمَنِ اضْطُرَّ فِىْ مَخْمَصَةٍ غَيْرَ مُتَجَانِفٍ لِّاِثْمٍۙ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏‏(3)\nHURREMAT A’LAYKOMUL MAYTATO WAD DAMO WA LAHMUL KHINZEERE WA MAA OHILLA LE-GHAYRIL LAAHE BEHI WAL MUNKHANEQATO WAL MAWQOOZATO WAL MOTARADDEYATO WAN NATEEHATO WA MAA AKALAS SABO-O’ ILLAA MAA ZAKKAYTUM, WA MAA ZOBEHA A’LAN NOSOBE WA AN TASTAQSEMOO BIL-AZLAAM, ZAALEKUM FISQ, AL-YAWMA YA-ESAL LAZEENA KAFAROO MIN DEENEKUM FALAA TAKHSHAWHUM WAKH SHAWN, AL-YAWMA AKMALTO LAKUM DEENAKUM WA ATMAMTO A’LAYKUM NE’MATEE WA RAZEETO LAKOMUL ISLAAMA DEENAA, FAMANIZ TURRA FEE MAKHMASATIN GHAYRA MOTAJAANEFIL LE-ISMIN, FA-INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nYou are prohibited carrion, blood, the flesh of swine, and what has been offered to other than Allah, and the animal strangled or beaten to death, and that which dies by falling or is gored to death, and that which is mangled by a beast of prey—barring that which you may purify —and what is sacrificed on stone altars [to idols], and that you should divide by raffling with arrows. All that is transgression. Today the faithless have despaired of your religion. So do not fear them, but fear Me. Today I have perfected your religion for you, and I have completed My blessing upon you, and I have approved Islam as your religion. But should anyone be compelled by hunger, without inclining to sin, then Allah is indeed all-forgiving, all-merciful.\nيَسْئَلُوْنَكَ مَاذَاۤ اُحِلَّ لَهُمْؕ قُلْ اُحِلَّ لَكُمُ الطَّيِّبٰتُ ۙ وَمَا عَلَّمْتُمْ مِّنَ الْجَوَارِحِ مُكَلِّبِيْنَ تُعَلِّمُوْنَهُنَّ مِمَّا عَلَّمَكُمُ اللّٰهُ فَكُلُوْا مِمَّاۤ اَمْسَكْنَ عَلَيْكُمْ وَاذْكُرُوا اسْمَ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْهِ وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ سَرِيْعُ الْحِسَابِ‏(4)\nYAS-ALOONAKA MAAZAA OHILLA LAHUM, QUL OHILLA LAKOMUT TAYYEBAATO, WA MAA A’LLAMTUM MENAL JAWAAREHE MOKALLEBEENA TO-A’LLEMOONAHUNNA MIMMAA A’LLAMAKOMUL LAAH, FA-KOLOO MIMMAA AMSAKNA A’LAYKUM WAZ KORUS MAL LAAHE A’LAYH, WAT TAQUL LAAH, INNAL LAAHA SAREE-U’L HESAAB.\nThey ask you as to what is lawful to them. Say, ‘All the good things are lawful to you.’ As for what you have taught hunting dogs [to catch], teaching them out of what Allah has taught you, eat of what they catch for you and mention Allah’s Name over it, and be wary of Allah. Indeed Allah is swift at reckoning.\nاَلْيَوْمَ اُحِلَّ لَكُمُ الطَّيِّبٰتُ ؕ وَطَعَامُ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوْا الْكِتٰبَ حِلٌّ لَّکُمْ وَطَعَامُكُمْ حِلٌّ لَّهُمْ وَالْمُحْصَنٰتُ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنٰتِ وَالْمُحْصَنٰتُ مِنَ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْكِتٰبَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ اِذَاۤ اٰتَيْتُمُوْهُنَّ اُجُوْرَهُنَّ مُحْصِنِيْنَ غَيْرَ مُسَافِحِيْنَ وَلَا مُتَّخِذِىْۤ اَخْدَانٍؕ وَمَنْ يَّكْفُرْ بِالْاِيْمَانِ فَقَدْ حَبِطَ عَمَلُهٗ وَهُوَ فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ مِنَ الْخٰسِرِيْنَ‏(5)\nAL-YAWMA OHILLA LAKOMUT TAYYEBAAT, WA TA-A’AMUL LAZEENA OOTUL KETAABA HILLUL LAKUM, WA TA-A’AMOKUM HILLUL LAHUM, WAL MOHSANAATO MENAL MOAMENAATE WAL MOHSANAATO MENAL LAZEENA OOTUL KETAABA MIN QABLEKUM EZAA AATAYTOMOOHUNNA OJOORAHUNNA MOHSENEENA GHAYRA MOSAAFEHEENA WA LAA MUTTAKHEZEE AKHDAAN, WA MAN-Y YAKFUR BIL-EEMAANE FAQAD HABETA A’MALOH, WA HOWA FIL AAKHERATE MENAL KHAASEREEN.\nToday all the good things have been made lawful to you—the food of those who were given the Book is lawful to you, and your food is lawful to them—and the chaste ones from among faithful women, and chaste women of those who were given the Book before you, when you have given them their dowries, in wedlock, not in license, nor taking paramours. Should anyone renounce his faith, his work shall fail and he will be among the losers in the Hereafter.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِذَا قُمْتُمْ اِلَى الصَّلٰوةِ فَاغْسِلُوْا وُجُوْهَكُمْ وَاَيْدِيَكُمْ اِلَى الْمَرَافِقِ وَامْسَحُوْا بِرُءُوْسِكُمْ وَاَرْجُلَكُمْ اِلَى الْكَعْبَيْنِ ؕ وَاِنْ كُنْتُمْ جُنُبًا فَاطَّهَّرُوْا ؕ وَاِنْ كُنْتُمْ مَّرْضَىٰۤ اَوْ عَلٰى سَفَرٍ اَوْ جَآءَ اَحَدٌ مِّنْكُمْ مِّنَ الْغَآئِطِ اَوْ لٰمَسْتُمُ النِّسَآءَ فَلَمْ تَجِدُوْا مَآءً فَتَيَمَّمُوْا صَعِيْدًا طَيِّبًا فَامْسَحُوْا بِوُجُوْهِكُمْ وَاَيْدِيْكُمْ مِّنْهُ ؕ مَا يُرِيْدُ اللّٰهُ لِيَجْعَلَ عَلَيْكُمْ مِّنْ حَرَجٍ وَّلٰكِنْ يُّرِيْدُ لِيُطَهِّرَكُمْ وَ لِيُتِمَّ نِعْمَتَهٗ عَلَيْكُمْ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(6)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO EZAA QUMTUM ELAS SALAATE FAGHSELOO WOJOOHAKUM WA AYDEYAKUM ELAL MARAAFEQE WAM SAHOO BE-RO-OOSEKUM WA ARJOLAKUM ELAL KA’BAYN, WA IN KUNTUM JONOBAN FAT-TAHHAROO, WA IN KUNTUM MARZAA AW A’LAA SAFARIN AW JAAA-A AHADUM MINKUM MENAL GHAAA-ETE AW LAAMASTOMUN NESAAA-A FALAM TAJEDOO MAAA-AN FA-TAYAMMAMOO SA-E’EDAN TAYYEBAN FAMSAHOO BE-WOJOOHEKUM WA AYDEEKUM MINH, MAA YOREEDUL LAAHO LE-YAJ-A’LA A’LAYKUM MIN HARAJINW WA LAAKIN-Y YOREEDO LE-YOTAHHERAKUM WA LE-YOTIMMA NE’MATAHU A’LAYKUM LA-A’LLAKUM TASHKOROON.\nO you who have faith! When you stand up for prayer, wash your faces and your hands up to the elbows, and wipe a part of your heads and your feet, up to the ankles. If you are junub, purify yourselves. But if you are sick, or on a journey, or any of you has come from the toilet, or you have touched women, and you cannot find water, then make tayammum with clean ground and wipe a part of your faces and your hands with it. Allah does not desire to put you to hardship, but He desires to purify you, and to complete His blessing upon you so that you may give thanks.\nوَاذْکُرُوْ انِعْمَةَ اللهِ عَلَیْکُمْ وَمِیْثَاقَهُ الَّذِیْ وَاثَقَکُمْ بِهۤ ۙ اِذْقُلْتُمْ سَمِعْنَا وَاَطَعْنَا وَاتَّقُوا اللهَ ؕ اِنَّ اللهَ عَلِیْمٌۢ بِذَاتِ الصُّدُوْرِ‏(7)\nWAZ KOROO NE’MATAL LAAHE A’LAYKUM WA MEESAAQAHUL LAZEE WAASAQAKUM BEHI, IZ QULTUM SAME’NAA WA ATA’NAA, WAT TAQUL LAAH, INNAL LAAHA A’LEEMUM BE-ZAATIS SODOOR.\nRemember Allah’s blessing upon you and His covenant with which He has bound you when you said, ‘We hear and obey.’ And be wary of Allah. Indeed Allah knows best what is in the breasts.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا كُوْنُوْا قَوَّا امِيْنَ لِلّٰهِ شُهَدَآءَ بِالْقِسْطِ وَلَا يَجْرِمَنَّكُمْ شَنَاٰنُ قَوْمٍ عَلٰٓى اَ لَّا تَعْدِلُوْا ؕ اِعْدِلُوْا هُوَ اَقْرَبُ لِلتَّقْوٰى وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ خَبِيْرٌۢ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(8)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO KOONOO QAWWAAMEENA LILLAAHE SHOHADAAA-A BIL-QIST, WA LAA YAJREMANNAKUM SHANA-AANO QAWMIN A’LAA ALLAA TA’DELOO, E-E’DELOO, HOWA AQRABO LIT-TAQWAA, WAT TAQUL LAAH, INNAL LAAHA KHABEERUM BEMAA TA’MALOON.\nO you who have faith! Be maintainers, as witnesses for the sake of Allah, of justice, and ill feeling for a people should never lead you to be unfair. Be fair; that is nearer to Godwariness, and be wary of Allah. Allah is indeed well aware of what you do.\nوَعَدَ اللّٰهُ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ ۙ لَهُمْ مَّغْفِرَةٌ وَّاَجْرٌ عَظِيْمٌ‏(9)\nWA-A’DAL LAAHUL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE, LAHUM MAGHFERATUNW WA AJRUN A’ZEEM.\nAllah has promised those who have faith and do righteous deeds forgiveness and a great reward.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَكَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَاۤ اُولٰٓئِكَ اَصْحٰبُ الْجَحِيْمِ‏(10)\nWAL LAZEENA KAFAROO WA KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA OOLAAA-EKA ASHAABUL JAHEEM.\nAs for those who are faithless and deny Our signs, they shall be the inmates of hell.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا اذْكُرُوْا نِعْمَتَ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْكُمْ اِذْ هَمَّ قَوْمٌ اَنْ يَّبْسُطُوْۤا اِلَيْكُمْ اَيْدِيَهُمْ فَكَفَّ اَيْدِيَهُمْ عَنْكُمْۚ وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ ؕ وَعَلَى اللّٰهِ فَلْيَتَوَكَّلِ الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(11)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANUZ KOROO NE’MATAL LAAHE A’LAYKUM IZ HAMMA QAWMUN AN-Y YABSOTOO ELAYKUM AYDEYAHUM FA-KAFFA AYDEYAHUM A’NKUM, WAT TAQUL LAAH, WA A’LAL LAAHE FALYATAWAKKALIL MOAMENOON.\nO you who have faith! Remember Allah’s blessing upon you when a people set out to extend their hands against you, but He withheld their hands from you, and be wary of Allah, and in Allah let all the faithful put their trust.\nوَلَقَدْ اَخَذَ اللّٰهُ مِيْثَاقَ بَنِىْۤ اِسْرآءِيْلَۚ وَبَعَثْنَا مِنْهُمُ اثْنَىْ عَشَرَ نَقِيْبًا ؕ وَقَالَ اللّٰهُ اِنِّىْ مَعَكُمْؕ لَئِنْ اَقَمْتُمُ الصَّلٰوةَ وَاٰتَيْتُمُ الزَّكٰوةَ وَاٰمَنْتُمْ بِرُسُلِىْ وَعَزَّرْتُمُوْهُمْ وَاَقْرَضْتُمُ اللّٰهَ قَرْضًا حَسَنًا لَّاُكَفِّرَنَّ عَنْكُمْ سَيِّاٰتِكُمْ وَلَاُدْخِلَنَّكُمْ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُۚ فَمَنْ كَفَرَ بَعْدَ ذٰ لِكَ مِنْكُمْ فَقَدْ ضَلَّ سَوَآءَ السَّبِيْلِ‏(12)\nWA LAQAD AKHAZAL LAAHO MEESAAQA BANEE ISRAAA-EEL, WA BA-A’SNAA MINHOMUS NAY A’SHARA NAQEEBAA, WA QAALAL LAAHO INNEE MA-A’KUM, LA-IN AQAMTOMUS SALAATA WA AATAYTOMUZ ZAKAATA WA AAMANTUM BE-ROSOLEE WA A’ZZARTOMOOHUM WA AQRAZTOMUL LAAHA QARZAN HASANAL LA-OKAFFERANNA A’NKUM SAYYE-AATEKUM WA LA-UDKHELANNAKUM JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAAR, FAMAN KAFARA BA’DA ZAALEKA MINKUM FAQAD ZALLA SAWAAA-AS SABEEL.\nCertainly Allah took a pledge from the Children of Israel, and We raised among them twelve chiefs. And Allah said, ‘I am with you! Surely, if you maintain the prayer and give the zakat and have faith in My apostles and support them and lend Allah a good loan, I will surely absolve you of your misdeeds, and I will surely admit you into gardens with streams running in them. But whoever of you disbelieves after that has certainly strayed from the right way.’\nفَبِمَا نَقْضِهِمْ مِّيْثَاقَهُمْ لَعَنّٰهُمْ وَجَعَلْنَا قُلُوْبَهُمْ قٰسِيَةً ۚ يُحَرِّفُوْنَ الْكَلِمَ عَنْ مَّوَاضِعِهٖۙ وَنَسُوْا حَظًّا مِّمَّا ذُكِّرُوْا بِهٖۚ وَلَا تَزَالُ تَطَّلِعُ عَلٰى خَآئِنَةٍ مِّنْهُمْ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا مِّنْهُمْ فَاعْفُ عَنْهُمْ وَاصْفَحْ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(13)\nFABEMAA NAQZEHIM MEESAAQAHUM LA-A’NNAAHUM WA JA-A’LNAA QOLOOBAHUM QAASEYAH, YOHARREFOONAL KALEMA A’M MAWAAZE-E’HI, WA NASOO HAZZAM MIMMAA ZUKKEROO BEH, WA LAA TAZAALO TATTALE-O’ A’LAA KHAAA-ENATIM MINHUM ILLAA QALEELAM MINHUM FA’FO A’NHUM WAS FAH, INNAL LAAHA YOHIBBUL MOHSENEEN.\nThen, because of their breaking their covenant We cursed them and made their hearts hard: they pervert words from their meanings, and have forgotten a part of what they were reminded. You will not cease to learn of some of their treachery, excepting a few of them. Yet excuse them and forbear. Indeed Allah loves the virtuous.\nوَمِنَ الَّذِيْنَ قَالُوْۤا اِنَّا نَصٰرٰٓى اَخَذْنَا مِيْثَاقَهُمْ فَنَسُوْا حَظًّا مِّمَّا ذُكِّرُوْا بِهٖ فَاَغْرَيْنَا بَيْنَهُمُ الْعَدَاوَةَ وَالْبَغْضَآءَ اِلٰى يَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِ ؕ وَسَوْفَ يُنَبِّئُهُمُ اللّٰهُ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَصْنَعُوْنَ‏(14)\nWA MENAL LAZEENA QAALOO INNAA NASAARAA AKHAZNAA MEESAAQAHUM FA-NASOO HAZZAM MIMMAA ZUKKEROO BEH, FA-AGHRAYNAA BAYNAHOMUL A’DAAWATA WAL BAGHZAAA-A ELAA YAWMIL QEYAAMAH, WA SAWFA YONABBE-OHOMUL LAAHO BEMAA KAANOO YASNA-O’ON.\nAlso from those who say, ‘We are Christians,’ We took their pledge; but they forgot a part of what they were reminded. So We stirred up enmity and hatred among them until the Day of Resurrection, and soon Allah will inform them concerning what they had been doing.\nيٰۤاَهْلَ الْكِتٰبِ قَدْ جَآءَكُمْ رَسُوْلُنَا يُبَيِّنُ لَكُمْ كَثِيْرًا مِّمَّا كُنْتُمْ تُخْفُوْنَ مِنَ الْكِتٰبِ وَيَعْفُوْا عَنْ كَثِيْرٍ ؕ قَدْ جَآءَكُمْ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ نُوْرٌ وَّكِتٰبٌ مُّبِيْنٌ ۙ‏(15)\nYAA AHLAL KETAABE QAD JAAA-AKUM RASOOLONAA YOBAYYENO LAKUM KASEERAM MIMMAA KUNTUM TUKHFOONA MENAL KETAABE WA YA’FOO A’N KASEER, QAD JAAA-AKUM MENAL LAAHE NOORUNW WA KETAABUM MOBEEN.\nO People of the Book! Certainly Our Apostle has come to you, clarifying for you much of what you used to hide of the Book, and excusing many [an offense of yours]. Certainly, there has come to you a light from Allah, and a manifest Book.\nيَّهْدِىْ بِهِ اللّٰهُ مَنِ اتَّبَعَ رِضْوَانَهٗ سُبُلَ السَّلٰمِ وَيُخْرِجُهُمْ مِّنَ الظُّلُمٰتِ اِلَى النُّوْرِ بِاِذْنِهٖ وَيَهْدِيْهِمْ اِلٰى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍ‏(16)\nYAHDEE BEHIL LAAHO MANIT TABA-A’ RIZWAANAHU SOBOLAS SALAAME WA YUKHREJOHUM MENAZ ZOLOMAATE ELAN NOORE BE-IZNEHI WA YAHDEEHIM ELAA SERAATIM MUSTAQEEM.\nWith it Allah guides those who follow [the course of] His pleasure to the ways of peace, and brings them out from darkness into light by His will, and guides them to a straight path.\nلَقَدْ كَفَرَ الَّذِيْنَ قَالُوْۤا اِنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ الْمَسِيْحُ ابْنُ مَرْيَمَؕ قُلْ فَمَنْ يَّمْلِكُ مِنَ اللّٰهِ شَيْئًا اِنْ اَرَادَ اَنْ يُّهْلِكَ الْمَسِيْحَ ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ وَاُمَّهٗ وَمَنْ فِى الْاَرْضِ جَمِيْعًا ؕ وَلِلّٰهِ مُلْكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا ؕ يَخْلُقُ مَا يَشَآءُ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(17)\nLAQAD KAFARAL LAZEENA QAALOO INNAL LAAHA HOWAL MASEEHUB NO MARYAM, QUL FAMAN-Y YAMLEKO MENAL LAAHE SHAY-AN IN ARAADA AN-Y YOHLEKAL MASEEHAB NA MARYAMA WA UMMAHU WA MAN FIL ARZE JAMEE-A’A, WA LILLAAHE MULKUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA, YAKHLOQO MAA YASHAAA, WAL LAAHO A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nThey are certainly faithless who say, ‘Allah is the Messiah, son of Mary.’ Say, ‘Who can avail anything against Allah should He wish to destroy the Messiah, son of Mary, and his mother, and everyone upon the earth?’ To Allah belongs the kingdom of the heavens and the earth, and whatever is between them. He creates whatever He wishes, and Allah has power over all things.\nوَقَالَتِ الْيَهُوْدُ وَالنَّصٰرٰى نَحْنُ اَبْنٰٓؤُا اللّٰهِ وَاَحِبَّآؤُهٗ ؕ قُلْ فَلِمَ يُعَذِّبُكُمْ بِذُنُوْبِكُمْؕ بَلْ اَنْتُمْ بَشَرٌ مِّمَّنْ خَلَقَ ؕ يَغْفِرُ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيُعَذِّبُ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ ؕ وَلِلّٰهِ مُلْكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا وَاِلَيْهِ الْمَصِيْرُ‏(18)\nWA QAALATIL YAHOODO WAN NASAARAA NAHNO ABNAAA-UL LAAHE WA AHIBBAAA-OH, QUL FALEMA YO-A’ZZEBOKUM BE-ZONOOBEKUM, BAL ANTUM BASHARUM MIMMAN KHALAQ, YAGHFERO LEMAN-Y YASHAAA-O WA YO-A’ZZEBO MAN-Y YASHAAA, WA LILLAAHE MULKUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA, WA ELAYHIL MASEER.\nThe Jews and the Christians say, ‘We are Allah’s children and His beloved ones.’ Say, ‘Then why does He punish you for your sins?’ No, you are humans from among His creatures. He forgives whomever He wishes, and punishes whomever He wishes, and to Allah belongs the kingdom of the heavens and the earth, and whatever is between them, and toward Him is the return.\nيٰۤاَهْلَ الْكِتٰبِ قَدْ جَآءَكُمْ رَسُوْلُنَا يُبَيِّنُ لَكُمْ عَلٰى فَتْرَةٍ مِّنَ الرُّسُلِ اَنْ تَقُوْلُوْا مَا جَآءَنَا مِنْۢ بَشِيْرٍ وَّلَا نَذِيْرٍ فَقَدْ جَآءَكُمْ بَشِيْرٌ وَّنَذِيْرٌؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(19)\nYAA AHLAL KETAABE QAD JAAA-AKUM RASOOLONAA YOBAYYENO LAKUM A’LAA FATRATIM MENAR ROSOLE AN TAQOOLOO MAA JAAA-ANAA MIM BASHEERINW WA LAA NAZEER, FAQAD JAAA-AKUM BASHEERUNW WA NAZEER, WAL LAAHO A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nO People of the Book! Certainly Our Apostle has come to you, clarifying [the Divine teachings] for you after a gap in [the appearance of] the apostles, lest you should say, ‘There did not come to us any bearer of good news nor any warner.’ Certainly, there has come to you a bearer of good news and a warner. And Allah has power over all things.\nوَاِذْ قَالَ مُوْسٰى لِقَوْمِهٖ يٰقَوْمِ اذْكُرُوْا نِعْمَةَ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْكُمْ اِذْ جَعَلَ فِيْكُمْ اَنْۢبِيَآءَ وَجَعَلَكُمْ مُّلُوْكًا  ۖ  وَّاٰتٰٮكُمْ مَّا لَمْ يُؤْتِ اَحَدًا مِّنَ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(20)\nWA IZ QAALA MOOSAA LE-QAWMEHI YAA QAWMIZ KOROO NE’MATAL LAAHE A’LAYKUM IZ JA-A’LA FEEKUM AMBEYAAA-A WA JA-A’LAKUM MOLOOKAA, WA AATAAKUM MAA LAM YOATE AHADAM MENAL A’ALAMEEN.\nWhen Moses said to his people, ‘O my people, remember Allah’s blessing upon you when He appointed prophets among you, and made you kings, and gave you what none of the nations were given.\nيٰقَوْمِ ادْخُلُوا الْاَرْضَ الْمُقَدَّسَةَ الَّتِىْ كَتَبَ اللّٰهُ لَكُمْ وَلَا تَرْتَدُّوْا عَلٰٓى اَدْبَارِكُمْ فَتَنْقَلِبُوْا خٰسِرِيْنَ‏(21)\nYAA QAWMID KHOLUL ARZAL MOQADDASATAL LATEE KATABAL LAAHO LAKUM WA LAA TARTADDOO A’LAA ADBAAREKUM FA-TANQALEBOO KHAASEREEN.\nO my people, enter the Holy Land which Allah has ordained for you, and do not turn your backs, or you will become losers.’\nقَالُوْا يٰمُوْسٰٓى اِنَّ فِيْهَا قَوْمًا جَبَّارِيْنَ ۖ  وَاِنَّا لَنْ نَّدْخُلَهَا حَتّٰى يَخْرُجُوْا مِنْهَا ۚ فَاِنْ يَّخْرُجُوْا مِنْهَا فَاِنَّا دَاخِلُوْنَ‏(22)\nQAALOO YAA MOOSAA INNA FEEHAA QAWMAN JABBAAREEN, WA INNAA LAN NADKHOLAHAA HATTAA YAKHROJOO MINHAA, FA-IN-Y YAKHROJOO MINHAA FA-INNAA DAAKHELOON.\nThey said, ‘O Moses, there are a tyrannical people in it. We will not enter it until they leave it. But once they leave it, we will go in.’\nقَالَ رَجُلٰنِ مِنَ الَّذِيْنَ يَخَافُوْنَ اَنْعَمَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِمَا ادْخُلُوْا عَلَيْهِمُ الْبَابَۚ فَاِذَا دَخَلْتُمُوْهُ فَاِنَّكُمْ غٰلِبُوْنَ  ۚ وَعَلَى اللّٰهِ فَتَوَكَّلُوْۤا اِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(23)\nQAALA RAJOLAANE MENAL LAZEENA YAKHAAFOONA AN-A’MAL LAAHO A’LAYHEMAD KHOLOO A’LAYHEMUL BAABA, FA-EZAA DAKHALTOMOOHO FA-INNAKUM GHAALEBOON, WA A’LAL LAAHE FATAWAKKALOO IN KUNTUM MOAMENEEN.\nSaid two men from among those who were Godfearing and whom Allah had blessed: ‘Go at them by the gate! For once, you have entered it, you will be victors. Put your trust in Allah, should you be faithful.’\nقَالُوْا يٰمُوْسٰٓى اِنَّا لَنْ نَّدْخُلَهَاۤ اَبَدًا مَّا دَامُوْا فِيْهَا فَاذْهَبْ اَنْتَ وَرَبُّكَ فَقَاتِلَاۤ اِنَّا هٰهُنَا قَاعِدُوْنَ‏(24)\nQAALOO YAA MOOSAA INNAA LAN NADKHOLAHAA ABADAM MAA DAAMOO FEEHAA FAZHAB ANTA WA RABBOKA FA-QAATELAA INNAA HAAHONAA QAA-E’DOON.\nThey said, ‘O Moses, we will never enter it so long as they remain in it. Go ahead, you and your Lord, and fight! We will be sitting right here.’\nقَالَ رَبِّ اِنِّىْ لَاۤ اَمْلِكُ اِلَّا نَفْسِىْ وَاَخِىْ فَافْرُقْ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَ الْقَوْمِ الْفٰسِقِيْنَ‏(25)\nQAALA RABBE INNEE LAA AMLEKO ILLAA NAFSEE WA AKHEE FAFRUQ BAYNANAA WA BAYNAL QAWMIL FAASEQEEN.\nHe said, ‘My Lord! I have no power over [anyone] except myself and my brother, so part us from the transgressing lot.’\nقَالَ فَاِنَّهَا مُحَرَّمَةٌ عَلَيْهِمْ اَرْبَعِيْنَ سَنَةً  ۚ يَتِيْهُوْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ ؕ فَلَا تَاْسَ عَلَى الْقَوْمِ الْفٰسِقِيْنَ‏(26)\nQAALA FA-INNAHAA MOHARRAMATUN A’LAYHIM ARBA-E’ENA SANAH, YATEEHOONA FIL ARZ, FALAA TAASA A’LAL QAWMIL FAASEQEEN.\nHe said, ‘It shall be forbidden them for forty years: they shall wander about in the earth. So do not grieve for the transgressing lot.’\nوَاتْلُ عَلَيْهِمْ نَبَاَ ابْنَىْ اٰدَمَ بِالْحَقِّۘ اِذْ قَرَّبَا قُرْبَانًا فَتُقُبِّلَ مِنْ اَحَدِهِمَا وَلَمْ يُتَقَبَّلْ مِنَ الْاٰخَرِؕ قَالَ لَاَقْتُلَنَّكَؕ قَالَ اِنَّمَا يَتَقَبَّلُ اللّٰهُ مِنَ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(27)\nWAT LO A’LAYHIM NABA-AB NAY AADAMA BIL-HAQ, IZ QARRABAA QURBAANAN FA-TOQUBBELA MIN AHADEHEMAA WA LAM YOTAQABBAL MENAL AAKHAR, QAALA LA-AQTOLANNAK, QAALA INNAMAA YATAQABBALUL LAAHO MENAL MUTTAQEEN.\nRelate to them truly the account of Adam’s two sons. When the two of them offered an offering, it was accepted from one of them and not accepted from the other. [One of them] said, ‘Surely I will kill you.’ [The other one] said, ‘Allah accepts only from the Godwary.\nلَئِنْۢ بَسَطْتَّ اِلَىَّ يَدَكَ لِتَقْتُلَنِىْ مَاۤ اَنَا بِبَاسِطٍ يَّدِىَ اِلَيْكَ لِاَقْتُلَكَ ۚ اِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ اللّٰهَ رَبَّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(28)\nLA-IM BASATTA ELAYYA YADAKA LE-TAQTOLANEE MAA ANAA BE-BAASETIN-Y YADEYA ELAYKA LE-AQTOLAK, INNEE AKHAAFUL LAAHA RABBAL A’ALAMEEN.\nEven if you extend your hand toward me to kill me, I will not extend my hand toward you to kill you. Indeed, I fear Allah, the Lord of all the worlds.\nاِنِّىْۤ اُرِيْدُ اَنْ تَبُوْٓءَ بِاِثْمِىْ وَ اِثْمِكَ فَتَكُوْنَ مِنْ اَصْحٰبِ النَّارِۚ وَذٰ لِكَ جَزٰٓؤُا الظّٰلِمِيْنَۚ‏‏(29)\nINNEE OREEDO AN TABOO-A BE-ISMEE WA ISMEKA FA-TAKOONA MIN ASHAABIN NAAR, WA ZAALEKA JAZAAA-UZ ZAALEMEEN.\nI desire that you earn [the burden of] my sin and your sin, to become one of the inmates of the Fire, and such is the requital of the wrongdoers.’\nفَطَوَّعَتْ لَهٗ نَفْسُهٗ قَتْلَ اَخِيْهِ فَقَتَلَهٗ فَاَصْبَحَ مِنَ الْخٰسِرِيْنَ‏(30)\nFA-TAWWA-A’T LAHU NAFSOHU QATLA AKHEEHE FA-QATALAHU FA-ASBAHA MENAL KHAASEREEN.\nSo his soul prompted him to kill his brother, and he killed him, and thus became one of the losers.\nفَبَعَثَ اللّٰهُ غُرَابًا يَّبْحَثُ فِىْ الْاَرْضِ لِيُرِيَهٗ كَيْفَ يُوَارِىْ سَوْءَةَ اَخِيْهِؕ قَالَ يَاوَيْلَتٰٓى اَعَجَزْتُ اَنْ اَكُوْنَ مِثْلَ هٰذَا الْغُرَابِ فَاُوَارِىَ سَوْءَةَ اَخِىْۚ فَاَصْبَحَ مِنَ النّٰدِمِيْنَۛ ۚ ۙ‏‏‏(31)\nFA-BA-A’SAL LAAHO GHORAABAN-Y YABHASO FIL ARZE LE-YOREYAHU KAYFA YOWAAREE SAW-ATA AKHEEH, QAALA YAA WAYLATAA A-A’JAZTO AN AKOONA MISLA HAAZAL GHORAABE FA-OWAAREYA SAW-ATA AKHEE, FA-ASBAHA MENAN NAADEMEEN.\nThen Allah sent a crow, exploring in the ground, to show him how to bury the corpse of his brother. He said, ‘Woe to me! Am I unable to be [even] like this crow and bury my brother’s corpse?’ Thus he became regretful.\nمِنْ اَجْلِ ذٰ لِكَ ۛ  ۚ كَتَبْنَا عَلٰى بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ اَنَّهٗ مَنْ قَتَلَ نَفْسًۢا بِغَيْرِ نَفْسٍ اَوْ فَسَادٍ فِى الْاَرْضِ فَكَاَنَّمَا قَتَلَ النَّاسَ جَمِيْعًا ؕ وَمَنْ اَحْيَاهَا فَكَاَنَّمَاۤ اَحْيَا النَّاسَ جَمِيْعًا ؕ وَلَقَدْ جَآءَتْهُمْ رُسُلُنَا بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ ثُمَّ اِنَّ كَثِيْرًا مِّنْهُمْ بَعْدَ ذٰ لِكَ فِى الْاَرْضِ لَمُسْرِفُوْنَ‏(32)\nMIN AJLE ZAALEK, KATABNAA A’LAA BANEE ISRAAA-EELA ANNAHU MAN QATALA NAFSAM BE-GHAYRE NAFSIN AW FASAADIN FIL ARZE FAKA-ANNAMAA QATALAN NAASA JAMEE-A’A, WA MAN AHYAAHAA FAKA-ANNAMAA AHYAN NAASA JAMEE-A’A, WA LAQAD JAAA-ATHUM ROSOLONAA BIL-BAYYENAAT, SUMMA INNA KASEERAM MINHUM BA’DA ZAALEKA FIL ARZE LA-MUSREFOON.\nThat is why We decreed for the Children of Israel that whoever kills a soul, without [its being guilty of] manslaughter or corruption on the earth, is as though he had killed all mankind, and whoever saves a life is as though he had saved all mankind. Our apostles certainly brought them manifest signs, yet even after that, many of them commit excesses on the earth.\nاِنَّمَا جَزٰٓؤُا الَّذِيْنَ يُحَارِبُوْنَ اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ وَيَسْعَوْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ فَسَادًا اَنْ يُّقَتَّلُوْۤا اَوْ يُصَلَّبُوْۤا اَوْ تُقَطَّعَ اَيْدِيْهِمْ وَاَرْجُلُهُمْ مِّنْ خِلَافٍ اَوْ يُنْفَوْا مِنَ الْاَرْضِؕ ذٰ لِكَ لَهُمْ خِزْىٌ فِى الدُّنْيَا وَ لَهُمْ فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ عَذَابٌ عَظِيْمٌ ۙ‏(33)\nINNAMAA JAZAAA-UL LAZEENA YOHAAREBOONAL LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU WA YAS-A’WNA FIL ARZE FASAADAN AN-Y YOQATTALOO AW YOSALLABOO AW TOQATTA-A’ AYDEEHIM WA ARJOLOHUM MIN KHELAAFIN AW YUNFAW MENAL ARZ, ZAALEKA LAHUM KHIZYUN FID DUNYAA WA LAHUM FIL AAKHERATE A’ZAABUN A’ZEEM.\nIndeed the requital of those who wage war against Allah and His Apostle, and try to cause corruption on the earth, is that they shall be slain or crucified, or shall have their hands and feet cut off from opposite sides, or be banished from the land. That is a disgrace for them in this world, and in the Hereafter, there is a great punishment for them,\nاِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ تَابُوْا مِنْ قَبْلِ اَنْ تَقْدِرُوْا عَلَيْهِمْۚ فَاعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(34)\nILLAL LAZEENA TAABOO MIN QABLE AN TAQDEROO A’LAYHIM, FA’LAMOO ANNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nexcepting those who repent before you capture them, and know that Allah is all-forgiving, all-merciful.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا اتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَابْتَغُوْۤا اِلَيْهِ الْوَسِيْلَةَ وَجَاهِدُوْا فِىْ سَبِيْلِهٖ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُوْنَ‏(35)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANUT TAQUL LAAHA WAB TAGHOO ELAYHIL WASEELATA WA JAAHEDOO FEE SABEELEHI LA-A’LLAKUM TUFLEHOON.\nO you who have faith! Be wary of Allah, and seek the means of recourse to Him, and wage jihad in His way, so that you may be felicitous.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لَوْ اَنَّ لَهُمْ مَّا فِى الْاَرْضِ جَمِيْعًا وَّمِثْلَهٗ مَعَهٗ لِيَفْتَدُوْا بِهٖ مِنْ عَذَابِ يَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِ مَا تُقُبِّلَ مِنْهُمْۚ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَ لِيْمٌ‏(36)\nINNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO LAW ANNA LAHUM MAA FIL ARZE JAMEE-A’NW WA MISLAHU MA-A’HU LE-YAFTADOO BEHI MIN A’ZAABE YAWMIL QEYAAMATE MAA TOQUBBELA MINHUM, WA LAHUM A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nIndeed if the faithless possessed all that is on the earth, and as much of it besides, to redeem themselves with it from the punishment of the Day of Resurrection, it shall not be accepted from them, and there is a painful punishment for them.\nيُرِيْدُوْنَ اَنْ يَّخْرُجُوْا مِنَ النَّارِ وَمَا هُمْ بِخَارِجِيْنَ مِنْهَا وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ مُّقِيْمٌ‏(37)\nYOREEDOONA AN-Y YAKHROJOO MENAN NAARE WA MAA HUM BE-KHAAREJEENA MINHAA, WA LAHUM A’ZAABUM MOQEEM.\nThey would long to leave the Fire, but they shall never leave it, and there is a lasting punishment for them.\nوَالسَّارِقُ وَالسَّارِقَةُ فَاقْطَعُوْۤا اَيْدِيَهُمَا جَزَآءًۢ بِمَا كَسَبَا نَكَالًا مِّنَ اللّٰهِ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَزِيْزٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(38)\nWAS SAAREQO WAS SAAREQATO FAQTA-O’O AYDEYAHOMAA JAZAAA-AM BEMAA KASABAA NAKAALAM MENAL LAAH, WAL LAAHO A’ZEEZUN HAKEEM.\nAs for the thief, man or woman, cut off their hands as a requital for what they have earned. [That is] an exemplary punishment from Allah, and Allah is all-mighty, all-wise.\nفَمَنْ تَابَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ ظُلْمِهٖ وَاَصْلَحَ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَتُوْبُ عَلَيْهِؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(39)\nFAMAN TAABA MIM BA’DE ZULMEHI WA ASLAHA FA-INNAL LAAHA YATOOBO A’LAYH, INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nBut whoever repents after his wrongdoing, and reforms, then Allah shall accept his repentance. Indeed Allah is all-forgiving, all-merciful.\nاَلَمْ تَعْلَمْ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ لَهٗ مُلْكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِؕ يُعَذِّبُ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيَغْفِرُ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(40)\nALAM TA’LAM ANNAL LAAHA LAHU MULKUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ, YO-A’ZZEBO MAN-Y YASHAAA-O WA YAGHFERO LEMAN-Y YASHAAA, WAL LAAHO A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nDo you not know that to Allah belongs the kingdom of the heavens and the earth? He punishes whomever He wishes, and forgives whomever He wishes, and Allah has power over all things.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الرَّسُوْلُ لَا يَحْزُنْكَ الَّذِيْنَ يُسَارِعُوْنَ فِى الْكُفْرِ مِنَ الَّذِيْنَ قَالُوْۤا اٰمَنَّا بِاَ فْوَاهِهِمْ وَلَمْ تُؤْمِنْ قُلُوْبُهُمْ ۛۚ وَمِنَ الَّذِيْنَ هَادُوْا  ۛۚ سَمّٰعُوْنَ لِلْكَذِبِ سَمّٰعُوْنَ لِقَوْمٍ اٰخَرِيْنَۙ لَمْ يَاْتُوْكَؕ يُحَرِّفُوْنَ الْكَلِمَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَوَاضِعِهٖۚ يَقُوْلُوْنَ اِنْ اُوْتِيْتُمْ هٰذَا فَخُذُوْهُ وَاِنْ لَّمْ تُؤْتَوْهُ فَاحْذَرُوْا ؕ وَمَنْ يُّرِدِ اللّٰهُ فِتْنَتَهٗ فَلَنْ تَمْلِكَ لَهٗ مِنَ اللّٰهِ شَيْئًاؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ لَمْ يُرِدِ اللّٰهُ اَنْ يُّطَهِّرَ قُلُوْبَهُمْ ؕ لَهُمْ فِىْ الدُّنْيَا خِزْىٌ ۚۖ وَّلَهُمْ فِىْ الْاٰخِرَةِ عَذَابٌ عَظِيْمٌ‏(41)\nYAA AYYOHAR RASOOLO LAA YAHZUNKAL LAZEENA YOSAARE-O’ONA FIL KUFRE MENAL LAZEENA QAALOO AAMANNAA BE-AFWAAHEHIM WA LAM TOAMIN QOLOOBOHUM, WA MENAL LAZEENA HAADOO, SAMMAA-O’ONA LIL-KAZEBE SAMMAA-O’ONA LE-QAWMIN AAKHAREENA, LAM YAATOOK, YOHARREFOONAL KALEMA MIM BA’DE MAWAAZE-E’H, YAQOOLOONA IN OOTEETUM HAAZAA FA-KHOZOOHO WA IL LAM TOATAWHO FAHZAROO, WA MAN-Y YOREDIL LAAHO FITNATAHU FALAN TAMLEKA LAHU MENAL LAAHE SHAY-AA, OOLAAA-EKAL LAZEENA LAM YOREDIL LAAHO AN-Y YOTAHHERA QOLOOBAHUM, LAHUM FID DUNYAA KHIZY, WA LAHUM FIL AAKHERATE A’ZAABUN A’ZEEM.\nO Apostle! Do not grieve for those who are active in [promoting] unfaith, such as those who say, ‘We believe’ with their mouths, but whose hearts have no faith, and the Jews who eavesdrop with the aim of [telling] lies [against you] and eavesdrop for other people who do not come to you. They pervert words from their meanings, [and] say, ‘If you are given this, take it, but if you are not given this, beware!’ Yet whomever Allah wishes to mislead, you cannot avail him anything against Allah. They are the ones whose hearts Allah did not desire to purify. For them is disgrace in this world, and there is a great punishment for them in the Hereafter.\nسَمّٰعُوْنَ لِلْكَذِبِ اَ كّٰلُوْنَ لِلسُّحْتِؕ فَاِنْ جَآءُوْكَ فَاحْكُمْ بَيْنَهُمْ اَوْ اَعْرِضْ عَنْهُمْ ۚ وَاِنْ تُعْرِضْ عَنْهُمْ فَلَنْ يَّضُرُّوْكَ شَيْئًا ؕ وَاِنْ حَكَمْتَ فَاحْكُمْ بَيْنَهُمْ بِالْقِسْطِ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُقْسِطِيْنَ‏(42)\nSAMMAA-O’ONA LIL-KAZEBE AKKAALOONA LIS-SOHT, FA-IN JAAA-OOKA FAHKUM BAYNAHUM AW A-A’RIZ A’NHUM, WA IN TO’RIZ A’NHUM FALAN-Y YAZURROOKA SHAY-AA, WA IN HAKAMTA FAHKUM BAYNAHUM BIL-QIST, INNAL LAAHA YOHIBBUL MUQSETEEN.\nEavesdroppers with the aim of [telling] lies, eaters of the unlawful—if they come to you, judge between them, or disregard them. If you disregard them, they will not harm you in any way. But if you judge, judge between them with justice. Indeed Allah loves the just.\nوَكَيْفَ يُحَكِّمُوْنَكَ وَعِنْدَهُمُ التَّوْرٰٮةُ فِيْهَا حُكْمُ اللّٰهِ ثُمَّ يَتَوَلَّوْنَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ ذٰ لِكَ ؕ وَمَاۤ اُولٰٓئِكَ بِالْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(43)\nWA KAYFA YOHAKKEMOONAKA WA I’NDAHOMUT TAWRAATO FEEHAA HUKMUL LAAHE SUMMA YATAWALLAWNA MIM BA’DE ZAALEK, WA MAA OOLAAA-EKA BIL-MOAMENEEN.\nAnd how should they make you a judge, while with them is the Torah, in which is Allah’s judgement? Yet in spite of that, they turn their backs [on Him] and they are not believers.\nاِنَّاۤ اَنْزَلْنَا التَّوْرٰٮةَ فِيْهَا هُدًى وَّنُوْرٌ ۚ يَحْكُمُ بِهَا النَّبِيُّوْنَ الَّذِيْنَ اَسْلَمُوْا لِلَّذِيْنَ هَادُوْا وَ الرَّبَّانِيُّوْنَ وَالْاَحْبَارُ بِمَا اسْتُحْفِظُوْا مِنْ كِتٰبِ اللّٰهِ وَكَانُوْا عَلَيْهِ شُهَدَآءَ ۚ فَلَا تَخْشَوُا النَّاسَ وَاخْشَوْنِ وَلَا تَشْتَرُوْا بِاٰيٰتِىْ ثَمَنًا قَلِيْلًا ؕ وَمَنْ لَّمْ يَحْكُمْ بِمَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ‏(44)\nINNAA ANZALNAT TAWRAATA FEEHAA HODANW WA NOOR, YAHKOMO BEHAN NABIYYOONAL LAZEENA ASLAMOO LILLAZEENA HAADOO WAR RABBAANIYYOONA WAL AHBAARO BEMAS TOHFEZOO MIN KETAABIL LAAHE WA KAANOO A’LAYHE SHOHADAAA, FALAA TAKHSHAWUN NAASA WAKH SHAWNE WA LAA TASHTAROO BE-AAYAATEE SAMANAN QALEELAA, WA MAL LAM YAHKUM BEMAA ANZALAL LAAHO FA-OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL KAAFEROON.\nWe sent down the Torah containing guidance and light. The prophets, who had submitted, judged by it for the Jews, and so did the rabbis and the scribes, as they were charged to preserve the Book of Allah and were witnesses to it. So do not fear the people, but fear Me, and do not sell My signs for a paltry gain. Those who do not judge by what Allah has sent down—it is they who are the faithless.\nوَكَتَبْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ فِيْهَاۤ اَنَّ النَّفْسَ بِالنَّفْسِۙ وَالْعَيْنَ بِالْعَيْنِ وَالْاَنْفَ بِالْاَنْفِ وَالْاُذُنَ بِالْاُذُنِ وَالسِّنَّ بِالسِّنِّۙ وَالْجُرُوْحَ قِصَاصٌؕ فَمَنْ تَصَدَّقَ بِهٖ فَهُوَ كَفَّارَةٌ لَّهٗ ؕ وَمَنْ لَّمْ يَحْكُمْ بِمَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ‏(45)\nWA KATABNAA A’LAYHIM FEEHAA ANNAN NAFSA BIN-NAFSE, WAL A’YNA BIL-A’YNE WAL ANFA BIL-ANFE WAL OZONA BIL-OZONE WAS SINNA BIS-SINNE, WAL JOROOHA QESAAS, FAMAN TASADDAQA BEHI FAHOWA KAFFAARATUL LAH, WA MAL LAM YAHKUM BEMAA ANZALAL LAAHO FA-OOLAAA-EKA HOMUZ ZAALEMOON.\nIn it We prescribed for them: a life for a life, an eye for an eye, a nose for a nose, and an ear for an ear, a tooth for a tooth, and retaliation for wounds. Yet whoever remits it out of charity, that shall be an atonement for him. Those who do not judge by what Allah has sent down—it is they who are the wrongdoers.\nوَقَفَّيْنَا عَلٰٓى اٰثَارِهِمْ بِعِيْسَى ابْنِ مَرْيَمَ مُصَدِّقًا لِّمَا بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ مِنَ التَّوْرٰٮةِ وَاٰتَيْنٰهُ الْاِنْجِيْلَ فِيْهِ هُدًى وَّنُوْرٌ ۙ وَّ مُصَدِّقًا لِّمَا بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ مِنَ التَّوْرٰٮةِ وَهُدًى وَّمَوْعِظَةً لِّلْمُتَّقِيْنَ ؕ‏(46)\nWA QAFFAYNAA A’LAA AASAAREHIM BE-E’ESAB NE MARYAMA MOSADDEQAL LEMAA BAYNA YADAYHE MENAT TAWRAAH, WA AATAYNAAHUL INJEELA FEEHE HODANW WA NOORUNW, WA MOSADDEQAL LEMAA BAYNA YADAYHE MENAT TAWRAATE WA HODANW WA MAW-E’ZATAL LIL-MUTTAQEEN.\nWe followed them with Jesus son of Mary, to confirm that which was before him of the Torah, and We gave him the Evangel containing guidance and light, confirming what was before it of the Torah, and as guidance and advice for the Godwary.\nوَلْيَحْكُمْ اَهْلُ الْاِنْجِيْلِ بِمَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ فِيْهِؕ وَمَنْ لَّمْ يَحْكُمْ بِمَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْفٰسِقُوْنَ‏(47)\nWAL YAHKUM AHLUL INJEELE BEMAA ANZALAL LAAHO FEEH, WA MAL LAM YAHKUM BEMAA ANZALAL LAAHO FA-OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL FAASEQOON.\nLet the people of the Evangel judge by what Allah has sent down in it. Those who do not judge by what Allah has sent down—it is they who are the transgressors.\nوَاَنْزَلْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ الْكِتٰبَ بِالْحَقِّ مُصَدِّقًا لِّمَا بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ مِنَ الْكِتٰبِ وَمُهَيْمِنًا عَلَيْهِ فَاحْكُمْ بَيْنَهُمْ بِمَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ وَلَا تَتَّبِعْ اَهْوَآءَهُمْ عَمَّا جَآءَكَ مِنَ الْحَقِّؕ لِكُلٍّ جَعَلْنَا مِنْكُمْ شِرْعَةً وَّمِنْهَاجًا ؕ وَلَوْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ لَجَعَلَكُمْ اُمَّةً وَّاحِدَةً وَّلٰكِنْ لِّيَبْلُوَكُمْ فِىْ مَاۤ اٰتٰٮكُمْ فَاسْتَبِقُوا الْخَيْرٰتِؕ اِلَى اللّٰهِ مَرْجِعُكُمْ جَمِيْعًا فَيُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ فِيْهِ تَخْتَلِفُوْنَۙ‏(48)\nWA ANZALNAA ELAYKAL KETAABA BIL-HAQQE MOSADDEQAL LEMAA BAYNA YADAYHE MENAL KETAABE WA MOHAYMENAN A’LAYHE FAHKUM BAYNAHUM BEMAA ANZALAL LAAHO WA LAA TATTABE’ AHWAAA-AHUM A’MMAA JAAA-AKA MENAL HAQ, LE-KULLIN JA-A’LNAA MINKUM SHIR-A’TANW WA MINHAAJAA, WA LAW SHAAA-AL LAAHO LAJA-A’LAKUM UMMATANW WAAHEDATANW WA LAAKIL LE-YABLOWAKUM FEE MAA AATAAKUM FASTABEQUL KHAYRAAT, ELAL LAAHE MARJE-O’KUM JAMEE-A’N FA-YONABBE-OKUM BEMAA KUNTUM FEEHE TAKHTALEFOON.\nWe have sent down to you the Book with the truth, confirming what was before it of the Book and as a guardian over it. So judge between them by what Allah has sent down, and do not follow their desires against the truth that has come to you. For each [community] among you We had appointed a code [of law] and a path, and had Allah wished He would have made you one community, but [His purposes required] that He should test you in respect to what He has given you. So take the lead in all good works. To Allah shall be the return of you all, whereat He will inform you concerning that about which you used to differ.\nوَاَنِ احْكُمْ بَيْنَهُمْ بِمَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ وَلَا تَتَّبِعْ اَهْوَآءَهُمْ وَاحْذَرْهُمْ اَنْ يَّفْتِنُوْكَ عَنْۢ بَعْضِ مَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ اِلَيْكَؕ فَاِنْ تَوَلَّوْا فَاعْلَمْ اَنَّمَا يُرِيْدُ اللّٰهُ اَنْ يُّصِيْبَهُمْ بِبَعْضِ ذُنُوْبِهِمْؕ وَاِنَّ كَثِيْرًا مِّنَ النَّاسِ لَفٰسِقُوْنَ‏(49)\nWA ANEH KUM BAYNAHUM BEMAA ANZALAL LAAHO WA LAA TATTABE’ AHWAAA-AHUM WAH ZARHUM AN-Y YAFTENOOKA A’M BA’ZE MAA ANZALAL LAAHO ELAYK, FA-IN TAWALLAW FA’LAM ANNAMAA YOREEDUL LAAHO AN-Y YOSEEBAHUM BE-BA’ZE ZONOOBEHIM, WA INNA KASEERAM MENAN NAASE LA-FAASEQOON.\nJudge between them by what Allah has sent down, and do not follow their desires. Beware of them lest they should beguile you from part of what Allah has sent down to you. But if they turn their backs [on you], then know that Allah desires to punish them for some of their sins, and indeed many of the people are transgressors.\nاَفَحُكْمَ الْجَاهِلِيَّةِ يَبْغُوْنَؕ وَمَنْ اَحْسَنُ مِنَ اللّٰهِ حُكْمًا لِّقَوْمٍ يُّوْقِنُوْنَ‏(50)\nAFA-HUKMAL JAAHELIYYATE YABGHOON, WA MAN AHSANO MENAL LAAHE HUKMAL LE-QAWMIN-Y YOOQENOON.\nDo they seek the judgement of [pagan] ignorance? But who is better than Allah in judgement for a people who have certainty?\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تَتَّخِذُوا الْيَهُوْدَ وَالنَّصٰرٰۤى اَوْلِيَآءَ ۘ بَعْضُهُمْ اَوْلِيَآءُ بَعْضٍؕ وَمَنْ يَّتَوَلَّهُمْ مِّنْكُمْ فَاِنَّهٗ مِنْهُمْؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(51)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA TATTAKHEZUL YAHOODA WAN NASAARAA AWLEYAAA, BA’ZOHUM AWLEYAAA-O BA’Z, WA MAN-Y YATAWALLAHUM MINKUM FA-INNAHU MINHUM, INNAL LAAHA LAA YAHDIL QAWMAZ ZAALEMEEN.\nO you who have faith! Do not take the Jews and the Christians for allies: they are allies of each other. Any of you who allies with them is indeed one of them. Indeed Allah does not guide the wrongdoing lot.\nفَتَرَى الَّذِيْنَ فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ مَّرَضٌ يُّسَارِعُوْنَ فِيْهِمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ نَخْشٰٓى اَنْ تُصِيْبَنَا دَآئِرَةٌ ؕ فَعَسَى اللّٰهُ اَنْ يَّاْتِىَ بِالْفَتْحِ اَوْ اَمْرٍ مِّنْ عِنْدِهٖ فَيُصْبِحُوْا عَلٰى مَاۤ اَسَرُّوْا فِىْۤ اَنْفُسِهِمْ نٰدِمِيْنَ ؕ‏(52)\nFA-TARAL LAZEENA FEE QOLOOBEHIM MARAZUN-Y YOSAARE-O’ONA FEEHIM YAQOOLOONA NAKHSHAA AN TOSEEBANAA DAAA-ERAH, FA-A’SAL LAAHO AN-Y YAATEYA BIL-FATHE AW AMRIM MIN I’NDEHI FA-YUSBEHOO A’LAA MAA ASARROO FEE ANFOSEHIM NAADEMEEN.\nYet you see those in whose hearts is a sickness rushing to them, saying, ‘We fear lest a turn of fortune should visit us.’ Maybe Allah will bring about a victory, or a command from Him, and then they will be regretful for what they kept secret in their hearts,\nوَيَقُوْلُ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اَهٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ الَّذِيْنَ اَقْسَمُوْا بِاللّٰهِ جَهْدَ اَيْمَانِهِمْۙ اِنَّهُمْ لَمَعَكُمْ ؕ حَبِطَتْ اَعْمَالُهُمْ فَاَصْبَحُوْا خٰسِرِيْنَ‏(53)\nWA YAQOOLUL LAZEENA AAMANOO AHAA-OLAAA-IL LAZEENA AQSAMOO BIL-LAAHE JAHDA AYMAANEHIM, INNAHUM LAMA-A’KUM, HABETAT A-A’MAALOHUM FA-ASBAHOO KHAASEREEN.\nand the faithful will say, ‘Are these the ones who swore by Allah with solemn oaths that they were with you?!’ Their works have failed, and they have become losers.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مَنْ يَّرْتَدَّ مِنْكُمْ عَنْ دِيْنِهٖ فَسَوْفَ يَاْتِى اللّٰهُ بِقَوْمٍ يُّحِبُّهُمْ وَيُحِبُّوْنَهٗۤ ۙ اَذِلَّةٍ عَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ اَعِزَّةٍ عَلَى الْكٰفِرِيْنَ يُجَاهِدُوْنَ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَلَا يَخَافُوْنَ لَوْمَةَ لَاۤئِمٍ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ فَضْلُ اللّٰهِ يُؤْتِيْهِ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ وَاسِعٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(54)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO MAN-Y YARTADDA MINKUM A’N DEENEHI FASAWFA YAATIL LAAHO BE-QAWMIN-Y YOHIBBOHUM WA YOHIBBOONAHU, AZILLATIN A’LAL MOAMENEENA A-I’ZZATIN A’LAL KAAFEREEN, YOJAAHEDOONA FEE SABEELIL LAAHE WA LAA YAKHAAFOONA LAWMATA LAAA-EM, ZAALEKA FAZLUL LAAHE YOATEEHE MAN-Y YASHAAA, WAL LAAHO WAASE-U’N A’LEEM.\nO you who have faith! Should any of you desert his religion, Allah will soon bring a people whom He loves and who love Him, [who will be] humble towards the faithful, stern towards the faithless, waging jihad in the way of Allah, not fearing the blame of any blamer. That is Allah’s grace, which He grants to whomever He wishes, and Allah is all-bounteous, all-knowing.\nاِنَّمَا وَلِيُّكُمُ اللّٰهُ وَرَسُوْلُهٗ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا الَّذِيْنَ يُقِيْمُوْنَ الصَّلٰوةَ وَيُؤْتُوْنَ الزَّكٰوةَ وَهُمْ رَاكِعُوْنَ‏(55)\nINNAMAA WALIYYOKOMUL LAAHO WA RASOOLOHU WAL LAZEENA AAMANUL LAZEENA YOQEEMOONAS SALAATA WA YOATOONAZ ZAKAATA WA HUM RAAKE-O’ON.\nYour guardian is only Allah, His Apostle, and the faithful who maintain the prayer and give the zakat while bowing down.\nوَمَنْ يَّتَوَلَّ اللّٰهَ وَ رَسُوْلَهٗ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا فَاِنَّ حِزْبَ اللّٰهِ هُمُ الْغٰلِبُوْنَ‏(56)\nWA MAN-Y YATAWALLAL LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO FA-INNA HIZBAL LAAHE HOMUL GHAALEBOON.\nWhoever takes for his guardians Allah, His Apostle and the faithful [should know that] the confederates of Allah are indeed the victorious.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تَتَّخِذُوا الَّذِيْنَ اتَّخَذُوْا دِيْنَكُمْ هُزُوًا وَّلَعِبًا مِّنَ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْكِتٰبَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ وَالْكُفَّارَ اَوْلِيَآءَ ۚ وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(57)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA TATTAKHEZUL LAZEENAT TAKHAZOO DEENAKUM HOZOWANW WA LA-E’BAM MENAL LAZEENA OOTUL KETAABA MIN QABLEKUM WAL KUFFAARA AWLEYAAA, WAT TAQUL LAAHA IN KUNTUM MOAMENEEN.\nO you who have faith! Do not take those who take your religion in derision and play, from among those who were given the Book before you, and the infidels, as friends, and be wary of Allah, should you be faithful.\nوَ اِذَا نَادَيْتُمْ اِلَى الصَّلٰوةِ اتَّخَذُوْهَا هُزُوًا وَّلَعِبًا ؕ ذٰ لِكَ بِاَنَّهُمْ قَوْمٌ لَّا يَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(58)\nWA EZAA NAADAYTUM ELAS SALAATIT TAKHAZOOHAA HOZOWANW WA LA-E’BAA, ZAALEKA BE-ANNAHUM QAWMUL LAA YA’QELOON.\nWhen you call to prayer, they take it in derision and play. That is because they are a people who do not exercise their reason.\nقُلْ يٰۤاَهْلَ الْكِتٰبِ هَلْ تَنْقِمُوْنَ مِنَّاۤ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ اٰمَنَّا بِاللّٰهِ وَمَاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْنَا وَمَاۤ اُنْزِلَ مِنْ قَبْلُ ۙ وَاَنَّ اَكْثَرَكُمْ فٰسِقُوْنَ‏(59)\nQUL YAA AHLAL KETAABE HAL TANQEMOONA MINNAA ILLAA AN AAMANNAA BIL-LAAHE WA MAA UNZELA ELAYNAA WA MAA UNZELA MIN QABLO, WA ANNA AKSARAKUM FAASEQOON.\nSay, ‘O People of the Book! Are you vindictive toward us for any reason except that we have faith in Allah and in what has been sent down to us, and in what was sent down before, and that most of you are transgressors?’\nقُلْ هَلْ اُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِشَرٍّ مِّنْ ذٰ لِكَ مَثُوْبَةً عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ ؕ مَنْ لَّعَنَهُ اللّٰهُ وَغَضِبَ عَلَيْهِ وَجَعَلَ مِنْهُمُ الْقِرَدَةَ وَالْخَنَازِيْرَ وَعَبَدَ الطَّاغُوْتَ ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ شَرٌّ مَّكَانًا وَّاَضَلُّ عَنْ سَوَآءِ السَّبِيْلِ‏(60)\nQUL HAL ONABBE-OKUM BE-SHARRIM MIN ZAALEKA MASOOBATAN I’NDAL LAAH, MAL LA-A’NAHUL LAAHO WA GHAZEBA A’LAYHE WA JA-A’LA MINHOMUL QERADATA WAL KHANAAZEERA WA A’BADAT TAAGHOOT, OOLAAA-EKA SHARRUM MAKAANANW WA AZALLO A’N SAWAAA-IS SABEEL.\nSay, ‘Shall I inform you concerning something worse than that as a requital from Allah? Those whom Allah has cursed and with whom He is wrathful, and turned some of whom into apes and swine, and worshippers of fake deities! Such are in a worse situation and more astray from the right way.’\nوَاِذَا جَآءُوْكُمْ قَالُوْۤا اٰمَنَّا وَقَدْ دَّخَلُوْا بِالْكُفْرِ وَهُمْ قَدْ خَرَجُوْا بِهٖؕ وَاللّٰهُ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَكْتُمُوْنَ‏(61)\nWA EZAA JAAA-OOKUM QAALOO AAMANNAA WA QAD DAKHALOO BIL-KUFRE WA HUM QAD KHARAJOO BEH, WAL LAAHO A-A’LAMO BEMAA KAANOO YAKTOMOON.\nWhen they come to you, they say, ‘We believe.’ Certainly, they enter with disbelief and leave with it, and Allah knows best as to what they have been concealing.\nوَتَرٰى كَثِيْرًا مِّنْهُمْ يُسَارِعُوْنَ فِى الْاِثْمِ وَالْعُدْوَانِ وَاَكْلِهِمُ السُّحْتَ ؕ لَبِئْسَ مَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(62)\nWA TARAA KASEERAM MINHUM YOSAARE-O’ONA FIL ISME WAL U’DWAANE WA AKLEHEMUS SOHT, LABEASA MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nYou see many of them actively engaged in sin and aggression, and consuming illicit gains. Surely, evil is what they have been doing.\nلَوْلَا يَنْهٰٮهُمُ الرَّبَّانِيُّوْنَ وَالْاَحْبَارُ عَنْ قَوْلِهِمُ الْاِثْمَ وَاَكْلِهِمُ السُّحْتَؕ لَبِئْسَ مَا كَانُوْا يَصْنَعُوْنَ‏(63)\nLAWLAA YANHAAHOMUR RABBAANIYYOONA WAL AHBAARO A’N QAWLEHEMUL ISMA WA AKLEHEMUS SOHT, LABEASA MAA KAANOO YASNA-O’ON.\nWhy do not the rabbis and the scribes forbid them from sinful speech and consuming illicit gains? Surely, evil is what they have been working.\nوَقَالَتِ الْيَهُوْدُ يَدُ اللّٰهِ مَغْلُوْلَةٌ ؕ غُلَّتْ اَيْدِيْهِمْ وَلُعِنُوْا بِمَا قَالُوْا ۘ بَلْ يَدٰهُ مَبْسُوْطَتٰنِ ۙ يُنْفِقُ كَيْفَ يَشَآءُ ؕ وَلَيَزِيْدَنَّ كَثِيْرًا مِّنْهُمْ مَّاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْكَ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ طُغْيَانًا وَّكُفْرًا ؕ وَاَ لْقَيْنَا بَيْنَهُمُ الْعَدَاوَةَ وَالْبَغْضَآءَ اِلٰى يَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِ ؕ كُلَّمَاۤ اَوْقَدُوْا نَارًا لِّلْحَرْبِ اَطْفَاَهَا اللّٰهُ ۙ وَيَسْعَوْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ فَسَادًا ؕ وَاللّٰهُ لَا يُحِبُّ الْمُفْسِدِيْنَ‏(64)\nWA QAALATIL YAHOODO YADUL LAAHE MAGHLOOLAH, GHULLAT AYDEEHIM WA LO-E’NOO BEMAA QAALOO, BAL YADAAHO MABSOOTATAANE, YUNFEQO KAYFA YASHAAA, WA LAYAZEEDANNA KASEERAM MINHUM MAA UNZELA ELAYKA MIR RABBEKA TUGHYAANANW WA KUFRAA, WA ALQAYNAA BAYNAHOMUL A’DAAWATA WAL BAGHZAAA-A ELAA YAWMIL QEYAAMAH, KULLAMAA AWQADOO NAARAL LIL-HARBE ATFA-AHAL LAAHO, WA YAS-A’WNA FIL ARZE FASAADAA, WAL LAAHO LAA YOHIBBUL MUFSEDEEN.\nThe Jews say, ‘Allah’s hand is tied up.’ Tied up be their hands, and cursed be they for what they say! No, His hands are wide open: He bestows as He wishes. Surely many of them will be increased in rebellion and unfaith by what has been sent to you from your Lord, and We have cast enmity and hatred amongst them until the Day of Resurrection. Every time they ignite the flames of war, Allah puts them out. They seek to cause corruption on the earth, and Allah does not like the agents of corruption.\nوَلَوْ اَنَّ اَهْلَ الْكِتٰبِ اٰمَنُوْا وَاتَّقَوْا لَكَفَّرْنَا عَنْهُمْ سَيِّاٰتِهِمْ وَلَاَدْخَلْنٰهُمْ جَنّٰتِ النَّعِيْمِ‏(65)\nWA LAW ANNA AHLAL KETAABE AAMANOO WAT TAQAW LAKAFFARNAA A’NHUM SAYYE-AATEHIM WA LA-ADKHALNAAHUM JANNAATIN NA-E’EM.\nHad the People of the Book believed and been Godwary, We would surely have absolved them of their misdeeds and admitted them into gardens of bliss.\nوَلَوْ اَنَّهُمْ اَقَامُوا التَّوْرٰٮةَ وَالْاِنْجِيْلَ وَمَاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْهِمْ مِّنْ رَّبِّهِمْ لَاَ كَلُوْا مِنْ فَوْقِهِمْ وَمِنْ تَحْتِ اَرْجُلِهِمْؕ مِنْهُمْ اُمَّةٌ مُّقْتَصِدَةٌ  ؕ وَكَثِيْرٌ مِّنْهُمْ سَآءَ مَا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(66)\nWA LAW ANNAHUM AQAAMUT TAWRAATA WAL INJEELA WA MAA UNZELA ELAYHIM MIR RABBEHIM LA-AKALOO MIN FAWQEHIM WA MIN TAHTE ARJOLEHIM, MINHUM UMMATUM MUQTASEDAH, WA KASEERUM MINHUM SAAA-A MAA YA’MALOON.\nHad they observed the Torah and the Evangel, and what was sent down to them from their Lord, they would surely have drawn nourishment from above them and from beneath their feet. There is an upright group among them, but evil is what many of them do.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الرَّسُوْلُ بَلِّغْ مَاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْكَ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ ؕ وَاِنْ لَّمْ تَفْعَلْ فَمَا بَلَّغْتَ رِسٰلَتَهٗ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ يَعْصِمُكَ مِنَ النَّاسِ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(67)\nYAA AYYOHAR RASOOLO BALLIGH MAA UNZELA ELAYKA MIR RABBEK, WA IL LAM TAF-A’L FAMAA BALLAGHTA RESAALATAH, WAL LAAHO YA’SEMOKA MENAN NAAS, INNAL LAAHA LAA YAHDIL QAWMAL KAAFEREEN.\nO Apostle! Communicate that which has been sent down to you from your Lord, and if you do not, you will not have communicated His message, and Allah shall protect you from the people. Indeed Allah does not guide the faithless lot.\nقُلْ يٰۤاَهْلَ الْكِتٰبِ لَسْتُمْ عَلٰى شَىْءٍ حَتّٰى تُقِيْمُوا التَّوْرٰٮةَ وَالْاِنْجِيْلَ وَمَاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْكُمْ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ ؕ وَلَيَزِيْدَنَّ كَثِيْرًا مِّنْهُمْ مَّاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْكَ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ طُغْيَانًا وَّكُفْرًاۚ فَلَا تَاْسَ عَلَى الْقَوْمِ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(68)\nQUL YAA AHLAL KETAABE LASTUM A’LAA SHAY-IN HATTAA TOQEEMUT TAWRAATA WAL INJEELA WA MAA UNZELA ELAYKUM MIR RABBEKUM, WA LAYAZEEDANNA KASEERAM MINHUM MAA UNZELA ELAYKA MIR RABBEKA TUGHYAANANW WA KUFRAA, FALAA TAASA A’LAL QAWMIL KAAFEREEN.\nSay, ‘O People of the Book! You do not stand on anything until you observe the Torah and the Evangel and what was sent down to you from your Lord.’ Surely many of them will be increased in rebellion and unfaith by what has been sent down to you from your Lord. So do not grieve for the faithless lot.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَالَّذِيْنَ هَادُوْا وَالصَّابِئُوْنَ وَالنَّصٰرٰى مَنْ اٰمَنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ وَعَمِلَ صَالِحًا فَلَا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا هُمْ يَحْزَنُوْنَ‏(69)\nINNAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WAL LAZEENA HAADOO WAS SAABE-OONA WAN NASAARAA MAN AAMANA BIL-LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHERE WA A’MELA SAALEHAN FALAA KHAWFUN A’LAYHIM WA LAA HUM YAHZANOON.\nIndeed the faithful, the Jews, the Sabaeans, and the Christians—those who have faith in Allah and the Last Day and act righteously—they will have no fear, nor will they grieve.\nلَقَدْ اَخَذْنَا مِيْثَاقَ بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ وَاَرْسَلْنَاۤ اِلَيْهِمْ رُسُلًا ؕ كُلَّمَا جَآءَهُمْ رَسُوْلٌ ۢ بِمَا لَا تَهْوٰٓى اَنْفُسُهُمْۙ فَرِيْقًا كَذَّبُوْا وَفَرِيْقًا يَّقْتُلُوْنَ‏(70)\nLAQAD AKHAZNAA MEESAAQA BANEE ISRAAA-EELA WA ARSALNAA ELAYHIM ROSOLAA, KULLAMAA JAAA-AHUM RASOOLUM BEMAA LAA TAHWAA ANFOSOHUM, FAREEQAN KAZZABOO WA FAREEQAN-Y YAQTOLOON.\nCertainly We took a pledge from the Children of Israel, and We sent apostles to them. Whenever an apostle brought them that which was not to their liking, they would impugn a part of them, and a part they would slay.\nوَحَسِبُوْۤا اَلَّا تَكُوْنَ فِتْنَةٌ فَعَمُوْا وَصَمُّوْا ثُمَّ تَابَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِمْ ثُمَّ عَمُوْا وَصَمُّوْا كَثِيْرٌ مِّنْهُمْؕ وَاللّٰهُ بَصِيْرٌۢ بِمَا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(71)\nWA HASEBOO ALLAA TAKOONA FITNATUN FA-A’MOO WA SAMMOO SUMMA TAABAL LAAHO A’LAYHIM SUMMA A’MOO WA SAMMOO KASEERUM MINHUM, WAL LAAHO BASEERUM BEMAA YA’MALOON.\nThey supposed there would be no testing, so they became blind and deaf. Thereafter Allah accepted their repentance, yet [again] many of them became blind and deaf, and Allah watches what they do.\nلَقَدْ كَفَرَ الَّذِيْنَ قَالُوْۤا اِنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ الْمَسِيْحُ ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ ؕ وَقَالَ الْمَسِيْحُ يٰبَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ اعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ رَبِّىْ وَرَبَّكُمْ ؕ اِنَّهٗ مَنْ يُّشْرِكْ بِاللّٰهِ فَقَدْ حَرَّمَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ الْجَنَّةَ وَمَاْوٰٮهُ النَّارُ ؕ وَمَا لِلظّٰلِمِيْنَ مِنْ اَنْصَارٍ‏(72)\nLAQAD KAFARAL LAZEENA QAALOO INNAL LAAHA HOWAL MASEEHUB NO MARYAM, WA QAALAL MASEEHO YAA BANEE ISRAAA-EELA’BODUL LAAHA RABBEE WA RABBAKUM, INNAHU MAN-Y YUSHRIK BIL-LAAHE FAQAD HARRAMAL LAAHO A’LAYHIL JANNATA WA MAAWAAHUN NAAR, WA MAA LIZ-ZAALEMEENA MIN ANSAAR.\nThey are certainly faithless who say, ‘Allah is the Messiah, son of Mary.’ But the Messiah had said, ‘O Children of Israel! Worship Allah, my Lord, and your Lord. Indeed whoever ascribes partners to Allah, Allah shall forbid him [entry into] paradise, and his refuge shall be the Fire, and the wrongdoers will not have any helpers.’\nلَقَدْ كَفَرَ الَّذِيْنَ قَالُوْۤا اِنَّ اللّٰهَ ثَالِثُ ثَلٰثَةٍ ۘ وَمَا مِنْ اِلٰهٍ اِلَّاۤ اِلٰهٌ وَّاحِدٌ  ؕ وَاِنْ لَّمْ يَنْتَهُوْا عَمَّا يَقُوْلُوْنَ لَيَمَسَّنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَ لِيْمٌ‏(73)\nLAQAD KAFARAL LAZEENA QAALOO INNAL LAAHA SAALESO SALAASAH, WA MAA MIN ELAAHIN ILLAA ELAAHUNW WAAHED, WA IL LAM YANTAHOO A’MMAA YAQOOLOONA LAYAMASSANNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO MINHUM A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nThey are certainly faithless who say, ‘Allah is the third [person] of a trinity,’ while there is no god except the One God. If they do not relinquish what they say, there shall befall the faithless among them a painful punishment.\nاَفَلَا يَتُوْبُوْنَ اِلَى اللّٰهِ وَيَسْتَغْفِرُوْنَهٗؕ وَاللّٰهُ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(74)\nAFALAA YATOOBOONA ELAL LAAHE WA YASTAGHFEROONAH, WAL LAAHO GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nWill they not repent to Allah and plead to Him for forgiveness? Yet Allah is all-forgiving, all-merciful.\nمَا الْمَسِيْحُ ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ اِلَّا رَسُوْلٌ ۚ قَدْ خَلَتْ مِنْ قَبْلِهِ الرُّسُلُؕ وَاُمُّهٗ صِدِّيْقَةٌ  ؕ كَانَا يَاْكُلٰنِ الطَّعَامَؕ اُنْظُرْ كَيْفَ نُبَيِّنُ لَهُمُ الْاٰيٰتِ ثُمَّ انْظُرْ اَ نّٰى يُؤْفَكُوْنَ‏(75)\nMAL MASEEHUB NO MARYAMA ILLAA RASOOL, QAD KHALAT MIN QABLEHIR ROSOL, WA UMMOHU SIDDEEQAH, KAANAA YAAKOLAANIT TA-A’AM, UNZUR KAYFA NOBAYYENO LAHOMUL AAYAATE SUMMAN ZUR ANNAA YOAFAKOON.\nThe Messiah, son of Mary, is but an apostle. Certainly, [other] apostles have passed before him, and his mother was a truthful one. Both of them would eat food. Look how We clarify the signs for them, and yet, look, how they go astray!\nقُلْ اَ تَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مَا لَا يَمْلِكُ لَكُمْ ضَرًّا وَّلَا نَفْعًا ؕ وَاللّٰهُ هُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(76)\nQUL ATA’BODOONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE MAA LAA YAMLEKO LAKUM ZARRANW WA LAA NAF-A’A, WAL LAAHO HOWAS SAMEE-U’L A’LEEM.\nSay, ‘Do you worship, besides Allah, what has no power to bring you any benefit or harm, while Allah—He is the All-hearing, the All-knowing?!’\nقُلْ يٰۤاَهْلَ الْكِتٰبِ لَا تَغْلُوْا فِىْ دِيْنِكُمْ غَيْرَ الْحَقِّ وَلَا تَتَّبِعُوْۤا اَهْوَآءَ قَوْمٍ قَدْ ضَلُّوْا مِنْ قَبْلُ وَاَضَلُّوْا كَثِيْرًا وَّضَلُّوْا عَنْ سَوَآءِ السَّبِيْلِ‏(77)\nQUL YAA AHLAL KETAABE LAA TAGHLOO FEE DEENEKUM GHAYRAL HAQQE WA LAA TATTABE-O’O AHWAAA-A QAWMIN QAD ZALLOO MIN QABLO WA AZALLOO KASEERANW WA ZALLOO A’N SAWAAA-IS SABEEL.\nSay, ‘O People of the Book! Do not unduly exceed the bounds in your religion and do not follow the fancies of a people who went astray in the past, and led many astray, and [themselves] strayed from the right path.’\nلُعِنَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْۢ بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ عَلٰى لِسَانِ دَاوٗدَ وَعِيْسَى ابْنِ مَرْيَمَ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ بِمَا عَصَوْا وَّكَانُوْا يَعْتَدُوْنَ‏(78)\nLO-E’NAL LAZEENA KAFAROO MIM BANEE ISRAAA-EELA A’LAA LESAANE DAAWOODA WA E’ESAB NE MARYAM, ZAALEKA BEMAA A’SAW WA KAANOO YA’TADOON.\nThe faithless among the Children of Israel were cursed on the tongue of David and Jesus son of Mary. That, because they would disobey and they used to commit transgression.\nكَانُوْا لَا يَتَنَاهَوْنَ عَنْ مُّنْكَرٍ فَعَلُوْهُ ؕ لَبِئْسَ مَا كَانُوْا يَفْعَلُوْنَ‏(79)\nKAANOO LAA YATANAAHAWNA A’M MUNKARIN FA-A’LOOH, LABEASA MAA KAANOO YAF-A’LOON.\nThey would not forbid one another from the wrongs that they committed. Surely, evil is what they had been doing.\nتَرٰى كَثِيْرًا مِّنْهُمْ يَتَوَلَّوْنَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْاؕ لَبِئْسَ مَا قَدَّمَتْ لَهُمْ اَنْفُسُهُمْ اَنْ سَخِطَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِمْ وَفِى الْعَذَابِ هُمْ خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(80)\nTARAA KASEERAM MINHUM YATAWALLAWNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO, LABEASA MAA QADDAMAT LAHUM ANFOSOHUM AN SAKHETAL LAAHO A’LAYHIM WA FIL A’ZAABE HUM KHAALEDOON.\nYou see many of them fraternizing with the faithless. Surely evil is what they have sent ahead for their souls, as Allah is displeased with them and they shall remain in punishment [forever].\nوَلَوْ كَانُوْا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَالنَّبِىِّ وَمَاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْهِ مَا اتَّخَذُوْهُمْ اَوْلِيَآءَ وَلٰكِنَّ كَثِيْرًا مِّنْهُمْ فٰسِقُوْنَ‏(81)\nWA LAW KAANOO YOAMENOONA BIL-LAAHE WAN NABIYYE WA MAA UNZELA ELAYHE MAT TAKHAZOOHUM AWLEYAAA-A WA LAAKINNA KASEERAM MINHUM FAASEQOON.\nHad they believed in Allah and the Prophet and what has been sent down to him, they would not have taken them for allies. But most of them are transgressors.\nلَتَجِدَنَّ اَشَدَّ النَّاسِ عَدَاوَةً لِّلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا الْيَهُوْدَ وَالَّذِيْنَ اَشْرَكُوْا ۚ وَلَتَجِدَنَّ اَ قْرَبَهُمْ مَّوَدَّةً لِّلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا الَّذِيْنَ قَالُوْۤا اِنَّا نَصٰرٰى ؕ ذٰ لِكَ بِاَنَّ مِنْهُمْ قِسِّيْسِيْنَ وَرُهْبَانًا وَّاَنَّهُمْ لَا يَسْتَكْبِرُوْنَ‏(82)\nLATAJEDANNA ASHADDAN NAASE A’DAAWATAL LILLAZEENA AAMANUL YAHOODA WAL LAZEENA ASHRAKOO, WA LATAJEDANNA AQRABAHUM MAWADDATAL LILLAZEENA AAMANUL LAZEENA QAALOO INNAA NASAARAA, ZAALEKA BE-ANNA MINHUM QISSEESEENA WA ROHBAANANW WA ANNAHUM LAA YASTAKBEROON.\nSurely You will find the most hostile of all people towards the faithful to be the Jews and the polytheists, and surely you will find the nearest of them in affection to the faithful to be those who say ‘We are Christians.’ That is because there are priests and monks among them, and because they are not arrogant.\nوَاِذَا سَمِعُوْا مَاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَى الرَّسُوْلِ تَرٰٓى اَعْيُنَهُمْ تَفِيْضُ مِنَ الدَّمْعِ مِمَّا عَرَفُوْا مِنَ الْحَقِّ‌ۚ يَقُوْلُوْنَ رَبَّنَاۤ اٰمَنَّا فَاكْتُبْنَا مَعَ الشّٰهِدِيْنَ‏(83)\nWA EZAA SAME-O’O MAA UNZELA ELAR RASOOLE TARAA A-A’YONAHUM TAFEEZO MENAD DAM-E’ MIMMAA A’RAFOO MENAL HAQ, YAQOOLOONA RABBANAA AAMANNAA FAKTUBNAA MA-A’SH SHAAHEDEEN.\nWhen they hear what has been revealed to the Apostle, you see their eyes fill with tears because of the truth that they recognize. They say, ‘Our Lord, we believe; so write us down among the witnesses.\nوَمَا لَنَا لَا نُؤْمِنُ بِاللّٰهِ وَمَا جَآءَنَا مِنَ الْحَقِّۙ وَنَطْمَعُ اَنْ يُّدْخِلَنَا رَبُّنَا مَعَ الْقَوْمِ الصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(84)\nWA MAA LANAA LAA NOAMENO BIL-LAAHE WA MAA JAAA-ANAA MENAL HAQQE, WA NATMA-O’ AN-Y YUDKHELANAA RABBONAA MA-A’L QAWMIS SAALEHEEN.\nWhy should we not believe in Allah and the truth that has come to us, eager as we are that our Lord should admit us among the righteous people?’\nفَاَثَابَهُمُ اللّٰهُ بِمَا قَالُوْا جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا‌ ؕ وَذٰ لِكَ جَزَآءُ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(85)\nFA-ASAABAHOMUL LAAHO BEMAA QAALOO JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA, WA ZAALEKA JAZAAA-UL MOHSENEEN.\nSo, for what they said, Allah requited them with gardens with streams running in them, to remain in them [forever], and that is the reward of the virtuous.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَكَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَاۤ اُولٰٓئِكَ اَصْحٰبُ الْجَحِيْمِ‏(86)\nWAL LAZEENA KAFAROO WA KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA OOLAAA-EKA ASHAABUL JAHEEM.\nBut those who are faithless and deny Our signs—they shall be the inmates of hell.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تُحَرِّمُوْا طَيِّبٰتِ مَاۤ اَحَلَّ اللّٰهُ لَكُمْ وَلَا تَعْتَدُوْا‌ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يُحِبُّ الْمُعْتَدِيْنَ‏(87)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA TOHARREMOO TAYYEBAATE MAA AHALLAL LAAHO LAKUM WA LAA TA’TADOO, INNAL LAAHA LAA YOHIBBUL MO’TADEEN.\nO you who have faith! Do not prohibit the good things that Allah has made lawful to you, and do not transgress. Indeed Allah does not like the transgressors.\nوَكُلُوْا مِمَّا رَزَقَكُمُ اللّٰهُ حَلٰلًا طَيِّبًا‌ وَّ اتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ الَّذِىْۤ اَنْتُمْ بِهٖ مُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(88)\nWA KOLOO MIMMAA RAZAQAKOMUL LAAHO HALAALAN TAYYEBAA, WAT TAQUL LAAHAL LAZEE ANTUM BEHI MOAMENOON.\nEat the lawful and good things Allah has provided you, and be wary of Allah in whom you have faith.\nلَا يُؤَاخِذُكُمُ اللّٰهُ بِاللَّغْوِ فِىْۤ اَيْمَانِكُمْ وَلٰكِنْ يُّؤَاخِذُكُمْ بِمَا عَقَّدْتُّمُ الْاَيْمَانَ‌ ۚ فَكَفَّارَتُهٗۤ اِطْعَامُ عَشَرَةِ مَسٰكِيْنَ مِنْ اَوْسَطِ مَا تُطْعِمُوْنَ اَهْلِيْكُمْ اَوْ كِسْوَتُهُمْ اَوْ تَحْرِيْرُ رَقَبَةٍ‌ ؕ فَمَنْ لَّمْ يَجِدْ فَصِيَامُ ثَلٰثَةِ اَيَّامٍ‌ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ كَفَّارَةُ اَيْمَانِكُمْ اِذَا حَلَفْتُمْ‌ ؕ وَاحْفَظُوْۤا اَيْمَانَكُمْ‌ ؕ كَذٰلِكَ يُبَيِّنُ اللّٰهُ لَكُمْ اٰيٰتِهٖ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(89)\nLAA YO-AAKHEZOKOMUL LAAHO BIL-LAGHWE FEE AYMAANEKUM WA LAAKIN-Y YO-AAKHEZOKUM BEMAA A’QQATTOMUL AYMAAN, FA-KAFFAARATOHU IT-A’AMO A’SHARATE MASAAKEENA MIN AWSATE MAA TUT-E’MOONA AHLEEKUM AW KISWATOHUM AW TAHREERO RAQABAH, FAMAL LAM YAJID FA-SEYAAMO SALAASATE AYYAAM, ZAALEKA KAFFAARATO AYMAANEKUM EZAA HALAFTUM, WAH FAZOO AYMAANAKUM, KAZAALEKA YOBAYYENUL LAAHO LAKUM AAYAATEHI LA-A’LLAKUM TASHKOROON.\nAllah shall not take you to task for what is frivolous in your oaths; but He shall take you to task for what you pledge in earnest. The atonement for it is to feed ten needy persons with the average food you give to your families, or their clothing, or the freeing of a slave. He who cannot afford [any of these] shall fast for three days. That is the atonement for your oaths when you vow. But keep your oaths. Thus does Allah clarify His signs for you so that you may give thanks.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِنَّمَا الْخَمْرُ وَالْمَيْسِرُ وَالْاَنْصَابُ وَالْاَزْلَامُ رِجْسٌ مِّنْ عَمَلِ الشَّيْطٰنِ فَاجْتَنِبُوْهُ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُوْنَ‏(90)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO INNAMAL KHAMRO WAL MAYSERO WAL ANSAABO WAL AZLAAMO RIJSUM MIN A’MALISH SHAYTAANE FAJTANEBOOHO LA-A’LLAKUM TUFLEHOON.\nO you who have faith! Indeed wine, gambling, idols, and the divining arrows are abominations of Satan’s doing, so avoid them, so that you may be felicitous.\nاِنَّمَا يُرِيْدُ الشَّيْطٰنُ اَنْ يُّوْقِعَ بَيْنَكُمُ الْعَدَاوَةَ وَالْبَغْضَآءَ فِى الْخَمْرِ وَالْمَيْسِرِ وَيَصُدَّكُمْ عَنْ ذِكْرِ اللّٰهِ وَعَنِ الصَّلٰوةِ‌ ۚ فَهَلْ اَنْتُمْ مُّنْتَهُوْنَ‏(91)\nINNAMAA YOREEDUSH SHAYTAANO AN-Y YOOQE-A’ BAYNAKOMUL A’DAAWATA WAL BAGHZAAA-A FIL KHAMRE WAL MAYSERE WA YASUDDAKUM A’N ZIKRIL LAAHE WA A’NIS SALAAH, FAHAL ANTUM MUNTAHOON.\nIndeed Satan seeks to cast enmity and hatred among you through wine and gambling, and to hinder you from the remembrance of Allah and from prayer. Will you, then, relinquish?\nوَاَطِيْعُوا اللّٰهَ وَاَطِيْعُوا الرَّسُوْلَ وَاحْذَرُوْا‌ ۚ فَاِنْ تَوَلَّيْتُمْ فَاعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّمَا عَلٰى رَسُوْلِنَا الْبَلٰغُ الْمُبِيْنُ‏(92)\nWA ATEE-U’L LAAHA WA ATEE-U’R RASOOLA WAH ZAROO, FA-IN TAWALLAYTUM FA’LAMOO ANNAMAA A’LAA RASOOLENAL BALAAGHUL MOBEEN.\nAnd obey Allah and obey the Apostle, and beware; but if you turn your backs, then know that Our Apostle’s duty is only to communicate in clear terms.\nلَيْسَ عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ جُنَاحٌ فِيْمَا طَعِمُوْۤا اِذَا مَا اتَّقَوا وَّاٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ ثُمَّ اتَّقَوا وَّاٰمَنُوْا ثُمَّ اتَّقَوا وَّاَحْسَنُوْا‌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ يُحِبُّ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(93)\nLAYSA A’LAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE JONAAHUN FEEMAA TA-E’MOO EZAA MAT TAQAW WA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE SUMMAT TAQAW WA AAMANOO SUMMAT TAQAW WA AHSANOO, WAL LAAHO YOHIBBUL MOHSENEEN.\nThere will be no sin upon those who have faith and do righteous deeds in regard to what they have eaten [in the past] so long as they are Godwary and faithful and do righteous deeds, and are further Godwary and faithful, and are further Godwary and virtuous. And Allah loves the virtuous.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَيَبْلُوَنَّكُمُ اللّٰهُ بِشَىْءٍ مِّنَ الصَّيْدِ تَنَالُهٗۤ اَيْدِيْكُمْ وَ رِمَاحُكُمْ لِيَعْلَمَ اللّٰهُ مَنْ يَّخَافُهٗ بِالْغَيْبِ‌ ۚ فَمَنِ اعْتَدٰى بَعْدَ ذٰ لِكَ فَلَهٗ عَذَابٌ اَ لِيْمٌ‏(94)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAYABLOWANNAKOMUL LAAHO BE-SHAY-IM MENAS SAYDE TANAALOHU AYDEEKUM WA REMAAHOKUM LE-YA’LAMAL LAAHO MAN-Y YAKHAAFOHU BIL-GHAYB, FAMANE’TADAA BA’DA ZAALEKA FALAHU A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nO you who have faith! Allah will surely test you with some of the game within the reach of your hands and spears, so that Allah may know those who fear Him in secret. So whoever transgresses after that, there is a painful punishment for him.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تَقْتُلُوا الصَّيْدَ وَاَنْتُمْ حُرُمٌ‌ ؕ وَمَنْ قَتَلَهٗ مِنْكُمْ مُّتَعَمِّدًا فَجَزَآءٌ مِّثْلُ مَا قَتَلَ مِنَ النَّعَمِ يَحْكُمُ بِهٖ ذَوَا عَدْلٍ مِّنْكُمْ هَدْيًاۢ بٰلِغَ الْكَعْبَةِ اَوْ كَفَّارَةٌ طَعَامُ مَسٰكِيْنَ اَوْ عَدْلُ ذٰ لِكَ صِيَامًا لِّيَذُوْقَ وَبَالَ اَمْرِهٖ‌ ؕ عَفَا اللّٰهُ عَمَّا سَلَفَ‌ ؕ وَمَنْ عَادَ فَيَنْتَقِمُ اللّٰهُ مِنْهُ‌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَزِيْزٌ ذُو انْتِقَامٍ‏(95)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA TAQTOLUS SAYDA WA ANTUM HOROM, WA MAN QATALAHU MINKUM MOTA-A’MMEDAN FA-JAZAAA-UM MISLO MAA QATALA MENAN NA-A’ME YAHKOMO BEHI ZAWAA A’DLIM MINKUM HADYAM BAALEGHAL KA’BATE AW KAFFAARATUN TA-A’AMO MASAAKEENA AW A’DLO ZAALEKA SEYAAMAL LE-YAZOOQA WABAALA AMREH, A’FAL LAAHO A’MMAA SALAF, WA MAN A’ADA FA-YANTAQEMUL LAAHO MINH, WAL LAAHO A’ZEEZUN ZUN TEQAAM.\nO you who have faith! Do not kill any game when you are in pilgrim sanctity. Should any of you kill it intentionally, its atonement, the counterpart from cattle of what he has killed, as judged by two fair men among you, will be an offering brought to the Ka‘bah, or an atonement by feeding needy persons, or its equivalent in fasting, that he may taste the untoward consequences of his conduct. Allah has excused what is already past; but should anyone resume, Allah shall take vengeance on him, for Allah is all-mighty, avenger.\nاُحِلَّ لَكُمْ صَيْدُ الْبَحْرِ وَطَعَامُهٗ مَتَاعًا لَّكُمْ وَلِلسَّيَّارَةِ‌ ۚ وَحُرِّمَ عَلَيْكُمْ صَيْدُ الْبَرِّ مَا دُمْتُمْ حُرُمًا‌ ؕ وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ الَّذِىْۤ اِلَيْهِ تُحْشَرُوْنَ‏(96)\nOHILLA LAKUM SAYDUL BAHRE WA TA-A’AMOHU MATAA-A’L LAKUM WA LIS-SAYYAARAH, WA HURREMA A’LAYKUM SAYDUL BARRE MAA DUMTUM HOROMAA, WAT TAQUL LAAHAL LAZEE ELAYHE TOHSHAROON.\nYou are permitted the game of the sea and its food, a provision for you and for the caravans, but you are forbidden the game of the land so long as you remain in pilgrim sanctity, and be wary of Allah toward whom you will be gathered.\nجَعَلَ اللّٰهُ الْكَعْبَةَ الْبَيْتَ الْحَرَامَ قِيٰمًا لِّلنَّاسِ وَالشَّهْرَ الْحَرَامَ وَالْهَدْىَ وَالْقَلَاۤئِدَ‌ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ لِتَعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ يَعْلَمُ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عَلِيْمٌ‏(97)\nJA-A’LAL LAAHUL KA’BATAL BAYTAL HARAAMA QEYAAMAL LIN-NAASE WASH SHAHRAL HARAAMA WAL HADYA WAL QALAAA-ED, ZAALEKA LE-TA’LAMOO ANNAL LAAHA YA’LAMO MAA FIS SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZE WA ANNAL LAAHA BE-KULLE SHAY-IN A’LEEM.\nAllah has made the Ka‘bah, the Sacred House, a [means of] sustentation for mankind, and [also] the sacred month, the offering and the garlands, so that you may know that Allah knows whatever there is in the heavens and whatever there is in the earth, and that Allah has knowledge of all things.\nاِعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ شَدِيْدُ الْعِقَابِ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ ؕ‏(98)\nE-E’LAMOO ANNAL LAAHA SHADEEDUL E’QAABE WA ANNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nKnow that Allah is severe in retribution, and that Allah is all-forgiving, all-merciful.\nمَا عَلَى الرَّسُوْلِ اِلَّا الْبَلٰغُ‌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ يَعْلَمُ مَا تُبْدُوْنَ وَمَا تَكْتُمُوْنَ‏(99)\nMAA A’LAR RASOOLE ILLAL BALAAGH, WAL LAAHO YA’LAMO MAA TUBDOONA WA MAA TAKTOMOON.\nThe Apostle’s duty is only to communicate and Allah knows whatever you disclose and whatever you conceal.\nقُلْ لَّا يَسْتَوِى الْخَبِيْثُ وَالطَّيِّبُ وَلَوْ اَعْجَبَكَ كَثْرَةُ الْخَبِيْثِ‌ ۚ فَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ يٰۤاُولِى الْاَ لْبَابِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُوْنَ‏(100)\nQUL LAA YASTAWIL KHABEESO WAT TAYYEBO WA LAW A-A’JABAKA KASRATUL KHABEES, FAT-TAQUL LAAHA YAA OOLIL ALBAABE LA-A’LLAKUM TUFLEHOON.\nSay, ‘The good and the bad are not equal, though the abundance of the bad should amaze you.’ So be wary of Allah, O you who possess intellect, so that you may be felicitous!\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تَسْئَلُوْا عَنْ اَشْيَآءَ اِنْ تُبْدَ لَكُمْ تَسُؤْكُمْ‌ۚ وَاِنْ تَسْئَلُوْا عَنْهَا حِيْنَ يُنَزَّلُ الْقُرْاٰنُ تُبْدَ لَكُمْ ؕ عَفَا اللّٰهُ عَنْهَا‌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ غَفُوْرٌ حَلِيْمٌ‏(101)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA TAS-ALOO A’N ASHYAAA-A IN TUBDA LAKUM TASOAKUM, WA IN TAS-ALOO A’NHAA HEENA YONAZZALUL QUR-AANO TUBDA LAKUM, A’FAL LAAHO A’NHAA, WAL LAAHO GHAFOORUN HALEEM.\nO you who have faith! Do not ask about things, which, if they are disclosed to you, will upset you. Yet if you ask about them while the Quran is being sent down, they shall be disclosed to you. Allah has excused it, and Allah is all-forgiving, all-forbearing.\nقَدْ سَاَ لَهَا قَوْمٌ مِّنْ قَبْلِكُمْ ثُمَّ اَصْبَحُوْا بِهَا كٰفِرِيْنَ‏(102)\nQAD SA-ALAHAA QAWMUM MIN QABLEKUM SUMMA ASBAHOO BEHAA KAAFEREEN.\nCertainly some people asked about them before you and then came to disbelieve in them.\nمَا جَعَلَ اللّٰهُ مِنْۢ بَحِيْرَةٍ وَّلَا سَآئِبَةٍ وَّلَا وَصِيْلَةٍ وَّلَا حَامٍ‌ ۙ وَّلٰكِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا يَفْتَرُوْنَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ الْكَذِبَ‌ ؕ وَاَكْثَرُهُمْ لَا يَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(103)\nMAA JA-A’LAL LAAHO MIM BAHEERATINW WA LAA SAAA-EBATINW WA LAA WASEELATINW WA LAA HAAMINW, WA LAAKINNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO YAFTAROONA A’LAL LAAHIL KAZEB, WA AKSAROHUM LAA YA’QELOON.\nAllah has not prescribed any such thing as Bahirah, Sa’ibah, Waseelah, or Haam; but those who are faithless fabricate lies against Allah, and most of them do not exercise their reason.\nوَاِذَا قِيْلَ لَهُمْ تَعَالَوْا اِلٰى مَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ وَاِلَى الرَّسُوْلِ قَالُوْا حَسْبُنَا مَا وَجَدْنَا عَلَيْهِ اٰبَآءَنَا‌ ؕ اَوَلَوْ كَانَ اٰبَآؤُهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ شَيْئًا وَّلَا يَهْتَدُوْنَ‏(104)\nWA EZAA QEELA LAHUM TA-A’ALAW ELAA MAA ANZALAL LAAHO WA ELAR RASOOLE QAALOO HASBONAA MAA WAJADNAA A’LAYHE AABAAA-ANAA, AWA LAW KAANA AABAAA-OHUM LAA YA’LAMOONA SHAY-ANW WA LAA YAHTADOON.\nWhen they are told, ‘Come to what Allah has sent down and [come] to the Apostle,’ they say, ‘Sufficient for us is what we have found our fathers following.’ What, even if their fathers did not know anything and were not guided?!\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا عَلَيْكُمْ اَنْفُسَكُمْ‌ۚ لَا يَضُرُّكُمْ مَّنْ ضَلَّ اِذَا اهْتَدَيْتُمْ‌ ؕ اِلَى اللّٰهِ مَرْجِعُكُمْ جَمِيْعًا فَيُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(105)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO A’LAYKUM ANFOSAKUM, LAA YAZURROKUM MAN ZALLA EZAH TADAYTUM, ELAL LAAHE MARJE-O’KUM JAMEE-A’N FA-YONABBE-OKUM BEMAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nO you who have faith! Take care of your own souls. He who strays cannot hurt you if you are guided. To Allah will be the return of you all, whereat He will inform you concerning what you used to do.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا شَهَادَةُ بَيْنِكُمْ اِذَا حَضَرَ اَحَدَكُمُ الْمَوْتُ حِيْنَ الْوَصِيَّةِ اثْنٰنِ ذَوَا عَدْلٍ مِّنْكُمْ اَوْ اٰخَرَانِ مِنْ غَيْرِكُمْ اِنْ اَنْتُمْ ضَرَبْتُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ فَاَصَابَتْكُمْ مُّصِيْبَةُ الْمَوْتِ‌ ؕ تَحْبِسُوْنَهُمَا مِنْۢ بَعْدِ الصَّلٰوةِ فَيُقْسِمٰنِ بِاللّٰهِ اِنِ ارْتَبْتُمْ لَا نَشْتَرِىْ بِهٖ ثَمَنًا وَّلَوْ كَانَ ذَا قُرْبٰى‌ ۙ وَلَا نَكْتُمُ شَهَادَةَ ۙ اللّٰهِ اِنَّاۤ اِذًا لَّمِنَ الْاٰثِمِيْنَ‏(106)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO SHAHAADATO BAYNEKUM EZAA HAZARA AHADAKOMUL MAWTO HEENAL WASIYYATIS NAANE ZAWAA A’DLIM MINKUM AW AAKHARAANE MIN GHAYREKUM IN ANTUM ZARABTUM FIL ARZE FA-ASAABATKUM MOSEEBATUL MAWT, TAHBESOONAHOMAA MIM BA’DIS SALAATE FA-YUQSEMAANE BIL-LAAHE ENIR TABTUM LAA NASHTAREE BEHI SAMANANW WA LAW KAANA ZAA QURBAA, WA LAA NAKTOMO SHAHAADATAL LAAHE INNAA EZAL LAMENAL AASEMEEN.\nO you who have faith! The witness between you, when death approaches any of you, while making a bequest, shall be two fair men from among yourselves—or two from among others, if you are journeying in the land and the affliction of death visits you. You shall detain the two of them after the prayer, and, if you have any doubt, they shall vow by Allah, ‘We will not sell it for any gain, even if it were a relative, nor will we conceal the testimony of Allah, for then we would indeed be among the sinners.’\nفَاِنْ عُثِرَ عَلٰٓى اَنَّهُمَا اسْتَحَقَّاۤ اِثْمًا فَاٰخَرٰنِ يَقُوْمٰنِ مَقَامَهُمَا مِنَ الَّذِيْنَ اسْتَحَقَّ عَلَيْهِمُ الْاَوْلَيٰنِ فَيُقْسِمٰنِ بِاللّٰهِ لَشَهَادَتُنَاۤ اَحَقُّ مِنْ شَهَادَتِهِمَا وَ مَا اعْتَدَيْنَاۤ‌ ‌ۖ  اِنَّاۤ‌ اِذًا لَّمِنَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(107)\nFA-IN O’SERA A’LAA ANNAHOMAS TAHAQQAA ISMAN FA-AAKHARAANE YAQOOMAANE MAQAAMAHOMAA MENAL LAZEENAS TAHAQQA A’LAYHEMUL AWLAYAANE FA-YUQSEMAANE BIL-LAAHE LA-SHAHAADATONAA AHAQQO MIN SHAHAADATEHEMAA WA MA’TADAYNAA, INNAA EZAL LAMENAZ ZAALEMEEN.\nBut if it is found that both of them were guilty of a sin, then two others shall stand up in their place from among those nearest in kinship to the claimants and swear by Allah: ‘Our testimony is surely truer than their testimony, and we have not transgressed, for then we would indeed be among the wrongdoers.’\nذٰ لِكَ اَدْنٰٓى اَنْ يَّاْتُوْا بِالشَّهَادَةِ عَلٰى وَجْهِهَاۤ اَوْ يَخَافُوْۤا اَنْ تُرَدَّ اَيْمَانٌۢ بَعْدَ اَيْمَانِهِمْ‌ؕ وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَاسْمَعُوْا‌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الْفٰسِقِيْنَ‏(108)\nZAALEKA ADNAA AN-Y YAATOO BISH-SHAHAADATE A’LAA WAJHEHAA AW YAKHAAFOO AN TORADDA AYMAANUM BA’DA AYMAANEHIM, WAT TAQUL LAAHA WAS MA-O’O, WAL LAAHO LAA YAHDIL QAWMAL FAASEQEEN.\nThat makes it likelier that they give the testimony in its genuine form, or fear that other oaths will be taken after their oaths. Be wary of Allah and listen, and Allah does not guide the transgressing lot.\nيَوْمَ يَجْمَعُ اللّٰهُ الرُّسُلَ فَيَقُوْلُ مَاذَاۤ اُجِبْتُمْ‌ ؕ قَالُوْا لَا عِلْمَ لَنَا ؕ اِنَّكَ اَنْتَ عَلَّامُ الْغُيُوْبِ‏(109)\nYAWMA YAJMA-U’L LAAHUR ROSOLA FA-YAQOOLO MAAZAA OJIBTUM, QAALOO LAA I’LMA LANAA, INNAKA ANTA A’LLAAMUL GHOYOOB.\nThe day Allah will gather the apostles and say, ‘What was the response to you?’ They will say, ‘We have no knowledge. Indeed You are knower of all that is Unseen.’\n‌اِذْ قَالَ اللّٰهُ يٰعِيْسَى ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ اذْكُرْ نِعْمَتِىْ عَلَيْكَ وَعَلٰى وَالِدَتِكَ‌ ۘ اِذْ اَيَّدتُّكَ بِرُوْحِ الْقُدُسِ تُكَلِّمُ النَّاسَ فِىْ الْمَهْدِ وَكَهْلًا ‌ ۚوَاِذْ عَلَّمْتُكَ الْكِتٰبَ وَالْحِكْمَةَ وَالتَّوْرٰٮةَ وَالْاِنْجِيْلَ‌ ۚ وَاِذْ تَخْلُقُ مِنَ الطِّيْنِ كَهَيْئَةِ الطَّيْرِ بِاِذْنِىْ فَتَنْفُخُ فِيْهَا فَتَكُوْنُ طَيْرًۢا بِاِذْنِىْ‌ وَ تُبْرِئُ الْاَكْمَهَ وَالْاَبْرَصَ بِاِذْنِىْ‌ ۚ وَاِذْ تُخْرِجُ الْمَوْتٰى بِاِذْنِىْ‌ ۚ وَاِذْ كَفَفْتُ بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ عَنْكَ اِذْ جِئْتَهُمْ بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ فَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْهُمْ اِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا سِحْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(110)\nIZ QAALAL LAAHO YAA E’ESAB NA MARYAMAZ KUR NE’MATEE A’LAYKA WA A’LAA WAALEDATEK, IZ AYYATTOKA BE-ROOHIL QODOS, TOKALLEMUN NAASA FIL MAHDE WA KAHLAA, WA IZ A’LLAMTOKAL KETAABA WAL HIKMATA WAT TAWRAATA WAL INJEEL, WA IZ TAKHLOQO MENAT TEENE KAHAY-ATIT TAYRE BE-IZNEE FA-TANFOKHO FEEHAA FA-TAKOONO TAYRAM BE-IZNEE WA TUBRE-UL AKMAHA WAL ABRASA BE-IZNEE, WA IZ TUKHREJUL MAWTAA BE-IZNEE, WA IZ KAFAFTO BANEE ISRAAA-EELA A’NKA IZ JEATAHUM BIL-BAYYENAATE FA-QAALAL LAZEENA KAFAROO MINHUM IN HAAZAA ILLAA SEHRUM MOBEEN.\nWhen Allah will say, O Jesus son of Mary, remember My blessing upon you and upon your mother, when I strengthened you with the Holy Spirit, so you would speak to the people in the cradle and in adulthood, and when I taught you the Book and wisdom, the Torah and the Evangel, and when you would create from clay the form of a bird, with My leave, and you would breathe into it and it would become a bird, with My leave; and you would heal the blind and the leper, with My leave, and you would raise the dead, with My leave; and when I held off [the evil of] the Children of Israel from you when you brought them manifest proofs, whereat the faithless among them said, ‘This is nothing but plain magic.’\nوَ اِذْ اَوْحَيْتُ اِلَى الْحَوَارِيّٖنَ اَنْ اٰمِنُوْا بِىْ وَبِرَسُوْلِىْ‌ۚ قَالُوْۤا اٰمَنَّا وَاشْهَدْ بِاَنَّنَا مُسْلِمُوْنَ‏(111)\nWA IZ AWHAYTO ELAL HAWAARIYYEENA AN AAMENOO BEE WA BE-RASOOLEE, QAALOO AAMANNAA WASH HAD BE-ANNANAA MUSLEMOON.\nAnd when I inspired the Disciples, [saying], ‘Have faith in Me and My apostle,’ they said, ‘We have faith. Bear witness that we are Muslims.’\nاِذْ قَالَ الْحَوَارِيُّوْنَ يٰعِيْسَى ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ هَلْ يَسْتَطِيْعُ رَبُّكَ اَنْ يُّنَزِّلَ عَلَيْنَا مَآئِدَةً مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ‌ ؕ قَالَ اتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(112)\nIZ QAALAL HAWAARIYYOONA YAA E’ESAB NA MARYAMA HAL YASTATEE-O’ RABBOKA AN-Y YONAZZELA A’LAYNAA MAAA-EDATAM MENAS SAMAAA, QAALAT TAQUL LAAHA IN KUNTUM MOAMENEEN.\nWhen the Disciples said, ‘O Jesus son of Mary! Can your Lord send down to us a table from the sky?’ Said he, ‘Be wary of Allah, should you be faithful.’\nقَالُوْا نُرِيْدُ اَنْ نَّاْكُلَ مِنْهَا وَتَطْمَئِنَّ قُلُوْبُنَا وَنَعْلَمَ اَنْ قَدْ صَدَقْتَنَا وَنَكُوْنَ عَلَيْهَا مِنَ الشّٰهِدِيْنَ‏(113)\nQAALOO NOREEDO AN NAAKOLA MINHAA WA TATMA-INNA QOLOOBONAA WA NA’LAMA AN QAD SADAQTANAA WA NAKOONA A’LAYHAA MENASH SHAAHEDEEN.\nThey said, ‘We desire to eat from it, and our hearts will be at rest: we shall know that you have told us the truth, and we shall be among the witnesses to it.’\nقَالَ عِيْسَى ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ اللّٰهُمَّ رَبَّنَاۤ اَنْزِلْ عَلَيْنَا مَآئِدَةً مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ تَكُوْنُ لَنَا عِيْدًا لِّاَوَّلِنَا وَاٰخِرِنَا وَاٰيَةً مِّنْكَ‌ۚ وَارْزُقْنَا وَاَنْتَ خَيْرُ الرّٰزِقِيْنَ‏(114)\nQAALA E’ESAB NO MARYAMAL LAAHUMMA RABBANAA ANZIL A’LAYNAA MAAA-EDATAM MENAS SAMAAA-E TAKOONO LANAA E’EDAL LE-AWWALENAA WA AAKHERENAA WA AAYATAM MINK, WAR ZUQNAA WA ANTA KHAYRUR RAAZEQEEN.\nSaid Jesus son of Mary, ‘O Allah! Our Lord! Send down to us a table from the sky, to be a festival for us, for the first ones and the last ones among us and as a sign from You, and provide for us; for You are the best of providers.’\nقَالَ اللّٰهُ اِنِّىْ مُنَزِّلُهَا عَلَيْكُمْ‌ۚ فَمَنْ يَّكْفُرْ بَعْدُ مِنْكُمْ فَاِنِّىْۤ اُعَذِّبُهٗ عَذَابًا لَّاۤ اُعَذِّبُهٗۤ اَحَدًا مِّنَ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(115)\nQAALAL LAAHO INNEE MONAZZELOHAA A’LAYKUM, FAMAN-Y YAKFUR BA’DO MINKUM FA-INNEE O-A’ZZEBOHU A’ZAABAL LAA O-A’ZZEBOHU AHADAM MENAL A’ALAMEEN.\nAllah said, ‘I will indeed send it down to you. But should any of you disbelieve after this, I will indeed punish him with a punishment such as I do not punish anyone in all creation.’\nوَاِذْ قَالَ اللّٰهُ يٰعِيْسَى ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ ءَاَنْتَ قُلْتَ لِلنَّاسِ اتَّخِذُوْنِىْ وَاُمِّىَ اِلٰهَيْنِ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ‌ؕ قَالَ سُبْحٰنَكَ مَا يَكُوْنُ لِىْۤ اَنْ اَقُوْلَ مَا لَيْسَ لِىْ بِحَقٍّ‌ؕ اِنْ كُنْتُ قُلْتُهٗ فَقَدْ عَلِمْتَهٗ‌ؕ تَعْلَمُ مَا فِىْ نَفْسِىْ وَلَاۤ اَعْلَمُ مَا فِىْ نَفْسِكَ‌ؕ اِنَّكَ اَنْتَ عَلَّامُ الْغُيُوْبِ‏(116)\nWA IZ QAALAL LAAHO YAA E’ESAB NA MARYAMA A-ANTA QULTA LIN-NAASIT TAKHEZOONEE WA UMMEYA ELAAHAYNE MIN DOONIL LAAH, QAALA SUBHAANAKA MAA YAKOONO LEE AN AQOOLA MAA LAYSA LEE, BE-HAQ, IN KUNTO QULTOHU FAQAD A’LIMTAH, TA’LAMO MAA FEE NAFSEE WA LAA A-A’LAMO MAA FEE NAFSEK, INNAKA ANTA A’LLAAMUL GHOYOOB.\nAnd when Allah will say, ‘O Jesus son of Mary! Was it you who said to the people, ‘‘Take me and my mother for gods besides Allah’’?’ He will say, ‘Immaculate are You! It does not behoove me to say what I have no right to [say]. Had I said it, You would certainly have known it: You know whatever is in my self, and I do not know what is in Your Self. Indeed, You are knower of all that is Unseen.\nمَا قُلْتُ لَهُمْ اِلَّا مَاۤ اَمَرْتَنِىْ بِهٖۤ اَنِ اعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ رَبِّىْ وَرَبَّكُمْ‌ۚ وَكُنْتُ عَلَيْهِمْ شَهِيْدًا مَّا دُمْتُ فِيْهِمْ‌ۚ فَلَمَّا تَوَفَّيْتَنِىْ كُنْتَ اَنْتَ الرَّقِيْبَ عَلَيْهِمْ‌ؕ وَاَنْتَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ شَهِيْدٌ‏(117)\nMAA QULTO LAHUM ILLAA MAA AMARTANEE BEHI ANE’BODUL LAAHA RABBEE WA RABBAKUM, WA KUNTO A’LAYHIM SHAHEEDAM MAA DUMTO FEEHIM, FALAMMAA TAWAFFAYTANEE KUNTA ANTAR RAQEEBA A’LAYHIM, WA ANTA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN SHAHEED.\nI did not say to them [anything] except what You had commanded me [to say]: ‘‘Worship Allah, my Lord and your Lord.’’ And I was a witness to them so long as I was among them. But when You had taken me away, You Yourself were watchful over them, and You are witness to all things.\nاِنْ تُعَذِّبْهُمْ فَاِنَّهُمْ عِبَادُكَ‌ۚ وَاِنْ تَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ فَاِنَّكَ اَنْتَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ‏(118)\nIN TO-A’ZZIBHUM FA-INNAHUM E’BAADOK, WA IN TAGHFIR LAHUM FA-INNAKA ANTAL A’ZEEZUL HAKEEM.\nIf You punish them, they are indeed Your creatures; but if You forgive them, You are indeed the All-mighty, the All-wise.’\nقَالَ اللّٰهُ هٰذَا يَوْمُ يَنْفَعُ الصّٰدِقِيْنَ صِدْقُهُمْ‌ؕ لَهُمْ جَنّٰتٌ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَاۤ اَبَدًا‌ ؕ رَضِىَ اللّٰهُ عَنْهُمْ وَرَضُوْا عَنْهُ‌ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيْمُ‏(119)\nQAALAL LAAHO HAAZAA YAWMO YANFA-U’S SAADEQEENA SIDQOHUM, LAHUM JANNAATUN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA ABADAA, RAZEYAL LAAHO A’NHUM WA RAZOO A’NH, ZAALEKAL FAWZUL A’ZEEM.\nAllah will say, ‘This day truthfulness shall benefit the truthful. For them there will be gardens with streams running in them, to remain in them forever. Allah is pleased with them and they are pleased with Him. That is the great success.’\nلِلّٰهِ مُلْكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَمَا فِيْهِنَّ‌ ؕ وَهُوَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(120)\nLILLAAHE MULKUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA MAA FEEHIN, WA HOWA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nTo Allah belongs the kingdom of the heavens and the earth and whatever there is in them, and He has power over all things.",
  "merits": "There are 120 verses in this Surah and it is a ‘Makki’ Surah i.e. it was revealed in Makkah. It is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that whoever recites this Surah, he will get a reward equivalent to ten times the number of Jews and Christians alive in the world, and will be forgiven the same amount of sins and will be raised in status by the same amount."
}
